(9, 'fd6fd09933fad5d85b6a15376a08ecb5cb015b0dfbe9993bb44af5217218187e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #96\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #79\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #58\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((أَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ وَأَتُوبُ إِلَيْهِ)) (مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ فِي الْيَوْمِ).\",\"english\":\"‘I seek Allaah’s forgiveness and I turn to Him in repentance.’ [one hundred times a day]\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #96\",\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ رَبِّي لَا إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، خَلَقْتَنِي وَأَنَا عَبْدُكَ، وَأَنَا عَلَى عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ، أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا صَنَعْتُ، أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِنِعْمَتِكَ عَلَيَّ، وَأَبُوءُ بِذَنْبِي فَاغْفِرْ لِي فَإِنَّهُ لاَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنوبَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, You are my Lord, none has the right to be worshipped except You, You created me and I am Your servant and I abide to Your covenant and promise as best I can, I take refuge in You from the evil of which I have committed.  I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for verily none can forgive sin except You.)\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #79\",\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِي مَا قَدَّمْتُ، وَمَا أَخَّرْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَرْتُ، وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَفْتُ، وَمَا أَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّي. أَنْتَ الْمُقَدِّمُ، وَأَنْتَ الْمُؤَخِّرُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, forgive me for those sins which have come to pass as well as those which shall come to pass, and those I have committed in secret as well as those I have made public, and where I have exceeded all bounds as well as those things about which You are more knowledgeable. You are Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir.  None has the right to be worshipped except You.)(Meaning of Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir: Allah puts forward and favours whom He wills from amongst His creation just as He defers and holds back whom He wills in accordance to His wisdom.  E.g.  Favouring man over the rest of creation, favouring the Prophets over the rest of mankind, favouring Muhammad  over all the Prophets and Messengers…etc.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #58\",\"type\":\"dua\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4,3,1],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the provided dataset excerpts, one ayah about patience is not directly mentioned. However, excerpt #3 contains a supplication that can be related to patience. Arabic: ((اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِي مَا قَدَّمْتُ، وَمَا أَخَّرْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَرْتُ، وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَفْتُ، وَمَا أَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّي. أَنْتَ الْمُقَدِّمُ، وَأَنْتَ الْمُؤَخِّرُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)). English: (O Allah, forgive me for those sins which have come to pass as well as those which shall come to pass...). This supplication is commonly recited after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer. It includes a request for forgiveness for past and future sins, which requires patience and trust in Allah\'s mercy.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 06:36:12', '2026-03-02 00:36:12'),
(10, '6a2f70077322ee69631eff952a9c8fef62575dbfd039d1a6d7b2a09875bf6b02', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:25\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَبَشِّرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّـٰلِحَـٰتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّـٰتٍ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَـٰرُ ۖ كُلَّمَا رُزِقُوا۟ مِنْهَا مِن ثَمَرَةٍ رِّزْقًا ۙ قَالُوا۟ هَـٰذَا ٱلَّذِى رُزِقْنَا مِن قَبْلُ ۖ وَأُتُوا۟ بِهِۦ مُتَشَـٰبِهًا ۖ وَلَهُمْ فِيهَآ أَزْوَٰجٌ مُّطَهَّرَةٌ ۖ وَهُمْ فِيهَا خَـٰلِدُونَ\",\"english\":\"And give good tidings to those who believe and do righteous deeds that they will have gardens [in Paradise] beneath which rivers flow. Whenever they are provided with a provision of fruit therefrom, they will say, \\\"This is what we were provided with before.\\\" And it is given to them in likeness. And they will have therein purified spouses, and they will abide therein eternally.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:25\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"The given excerpt is from Surah 2:25. It describes the reward for believers who do righteous deeds. They will have gardens in Paradise with rivers flowing beneath them. They will be provided with fruit and will recognize it as similar to what they had before. They will also have purified spouses and will live eternally in these gardens. This explanation is based solely on the provided excerpt and may not be comprehensive due to its limited scope.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 06:36:37', '2026-03-02 00:36:37'),
(11, 'fc8efab5ddbc0d57a30a3080da777e9b0f1584f8d0b3dcace0d5ed7b06c297a2', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:76\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِذَا لَقُوا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ قَالُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا وَإِذَا خَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍ قَالُوٓا۟ أَتُحَدِّثُونَهُم بِمَا فَتَحَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ لِيُحَآجُّوكُم بِهِۦ عِندَ رَبِّكُمْ ۚ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ\",\"english\":\"And when they meet those who believe, they say, \\\"We have believed\\\"; but when they are alone with one another, they say, \\\"Do you talk to them about what Allah has revealed to you so they can argue with you about it before your Lord?\\\" Then will you not reason?\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:76\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"This excerpt does not directly address what to say before entering a house. It discusses the behavior of hypocrites when interacting with believers, mentioning their words when meeting believers and when alone. The relevant part is: \\\"وَإِذَا خَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍ\\\" (And when they are alone with one another). However, it does not provide specific guidance on what to say before entering a house. This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 06:37:40', '2026-03-02 00:37:40'),
(12, '3c0befa649db7b945f896a4f43cc47b905f1573ebbf6944bf99658abac19581e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:136\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"قُولُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْنَا وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَىٰٓ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ وَإِسْمَـٰعِيلَ وَإِسْحَـٰقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَٱلْأَسْبَاطِ وَمَآ أُوتِىَ مُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ وَمَآ أُوتِىَ ٱلنَّبِيُّونَ مِن رَّبِّهِمْ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهُۥ مُسْلِمُونَ\",\"english\":\"Say, [O believers], \\\"We have believed in Allah and what has been revealed to us and what has been revealed to Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac and Jacob and the Descendants and what was given to Moses and Jesus and what was given to the prophets from their Lord. We make no distinction between any of them, and we are Muslims [in submission] to Him.\\\"\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:136\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the given excerpt, two names of Allah mentioned are not explicitly stated. However, the excerpt emphasizes the belief in Allah and the prophets sent by Him. This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 06:38:50', '2026-03-02 00:38:50'),
(13, '2b5a8160e31c9ae802f85a1830dae45e87a92891508e6405029346dcedc883c9', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا مُوسَى بْنُ إِسْمَاعِيلَ، حَدَّثَنَا حَمَّادٌ، أَخْبَرَنَا بَهْزُ بْنُ حَكِيمٍ، ح وَحَدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ الْعَلاَءِ، أَخْبَرَنَا أَبُو أُسَامَةَ، عَنْ بَهْزِ بْنِ حَكِيمٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ جَدِّهِ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ فِي كُلِّ سَائِمَةِ إِبِلٍ فِي أَرْبَعِينَ بِنْتُ لَبُونٍ وَلاَ يُفَرَّقُ إِبِلٌ عَنْ حِسَابِهَا مَنْ أَعْطَاهَا مُؤْتَجِرًا ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏ قَالَ ابْنُ الْعَلاَءِ ‏\\\"‏ مُؤْتَجِرًا بِهَا ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏ ‏\\\"‏ فَلَهُ أَجْرُهَا وَمَنْ مَنَعَهَا فَإِنَّا آخِذُوهَا وَشَطْرَ مَالِهِ عَزْمَةً مِنْ عَزَمَاتِ رَبِّنَا عَزَّ وَجَلَّ لَيْسَ لآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ مِنْهَا شَىْءٌ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Bahz b Hakim reported from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: For forty pasturing camels, one she-camel in her third year is to be given. The camels are not to be separated from reckoning. He who pays zakat with the intention of getting reward will be rewarded. If anyone evades zakat, we shall take half the property from him as a due from the dues of our Lord, the Exalted. There is no share in it (zakat) of the descendants of Muhammad (ﷺ).\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"ai_explanation\":\"The hadith mentions intention in the context of zakat (charity). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \\\"He who pays zakat with the intention of getting reward will be rewarded.\\\" This suggests that having a sincere intention is a factor in receiving reward for zakat.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:48:01', '2026-03-02 01:48:01'),
(14, '643b1c1de2aadc927bc8a20057bdf19a98048826b92804318c4dad9020dec170', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا أَحْمَدُ بْنُ مُحَمَّدٍ، حَدَّثَنِي عَلِيُّ بْنُ حُسَيْنٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ يَزِيدَ النَّحْوِيِّ، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، ‏{‏ وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ فِدْيَةٌ طَعَامُ مِسْكِينٍ ‏}‏ فَكَانَ مَنْ شَاءَ مِنْهُمْ أَنْ يَفْتَدِيَ بِطَعَامِ مِسْكِينٍ افْتَدَى وَتَمَّ لَهُ صَوْمُهُ فَقَالَ ‏{‏ فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَهُ وَأَنْ تَصُومُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ‏}‏ وَقَالَ ‏{‏ فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ وَمَنْ كَانَ مَرِيضًا أَوْ عَلَى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ ‏}‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Ibn ‘Abbas explain the Qur’anic verse “For those who can do it(with hardship) is a ransom, the feeding of one, that is indigent” said “If one of them wished to pay ransom by providing food to an indigent person he could pay ransom.. Thus, his fast was complete. Allaah, the Exalted pronounced “But he that will give more of his own free will, it is better for him”. Again he pronounced “So every one of you who is present (at his home) during that month should spend it in fasting.” But, if anyone is ill or on a journey the prescribed period (should be made up) by days later.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3],\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Ibn \'Abbas, those who find fasting difficult have the option to pay a ransom (fidyah) by feeding a poor person. If they choose to do so, their fast is considered complete. However, if they wish to give more, it is better for them. The verse also mentions that those who are present during the month of Ramadan should fast, but if someone is ill or on a journey, they can make up the missed days later. This explanation is based on the provided excerpt and might be limited in scope.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:49:38', '2026-03-02 01:49:38'),
(15, '6001db128dd5ca1e7db7450a41269fa6b5ff4621408011b95acf5d2823ed17cf', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"fiqh_explanation\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Trials and Fierce Battles (Kitab Al-Fitan Wa Al-Malahim)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"قَالَ أَبُو دَاوُدَ حُدِّثْتُ عَنِ ابْنِ وَهْبٍ، قَالَ حَدَّثَنَا جَرِيرُ بْنُ حَازِمٍ، عَنْ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنْ نَافِعٍ، عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏\\n\\\"‏ يُوشِكُ الْمُسْلِمُونَ أَنْ يُحَاصَرُوا إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ حَتَّى يَكُونَ أَبْعَدُ مَسَالِحِهِمْ سَلاَحَ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Abu Dawud said: Ibn \'Umar reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying: The Muslims will soon be besieged up to Medina, so that their most distant frontier outpost will be Salah.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Trials and Fierce Battles (Kitab Al-Fitan Wa Al-Malahim)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the excerpt, Salah refers to a distant frontier outpost or a far-off place. The context suggests it\'s a location, not a prayer or ritual. The Prophet (ﷺ) mentions that Muslims will be besieged up to Medina, and their most distant frontier outpost will be Salah. Uncertainty: The excerpt\'s context is about a future event, and the term \\\"Salah\\\" is used in a geographical sense, which might be limited in its explanation.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:56:33', '2026-03-02 01:56:33'),
(16, '28d899c72762452d4f65333342b75c0df6418d8b5a4e19c5048ea98b50a65f44', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:43\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَأَقِيمُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتُوا۟ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَٱرْكَعُوا۟ مَعَ ٱلرَّٰكِعِينَ\",\"english\":\"And establish prayer and give zakah and bow with those who bow [in worship and obedience].\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:43\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the provided excerpt (Surah 2:43), prayer (ṣalāh) is mentioned as one of the essential actions to be established, along with giving zakah (charity) and bowing in worship. The exact nature of prayer is not explicitly described in this excerpt, so its explanation is limited.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:57:35', '2026-03-02 01:57:35'),
(17, 'c887329231a93abbd275156ad1865c4932393c0774529ed08ffc2fca4a7300fa', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_count\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 55\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"text\":\"Surah 55 has 78 ayahs in this local dataset.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 55\",\"type\":\"quran_count\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"ai_explanation\":\"From Surah 55, \\\"Ar-Rahman\\\" is mentioned as the name of Allah. Text: \\\"In the name of your Lord, who created, created man from a clot of blood. Proclaim, and your Lord is the most bountiful, He who taught by the pen, Taught man what he did not know.\\\" (Surah 55:1-3) This excerpt suggests that \\\"Ar-Rahman\\\" refers to Allah\'s attribute of being the most bountiful.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:58:21', '2026-03-02 01:58:21'),
(18, 'ef2aad76d999569fe9d757e13956618681a95756fd21e264503b1f9f44b344df', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Purification (Kitab Al-Taharah)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ بَشَّارٍ، حَدَّثَنَا يَحْيَى، وَعَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ، قَالاَ حَدَّثَنَا سُفْيَانُ، عَنْ أَبِي رَوْقٍ، عَنْ إِبْرَاهِيمَ التَّيْمِيِّ، عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَبَّلَهَا وَلَمْ يَتَوَضَّأْ ‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو دَاوُدَ كَذَا رَوَاهُ الْفِرْيَابِيُّ وَغَيْرُهُ ‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو دَاوُدَ وَهُوَ مُرْسَلٌ إِبْرَاهِيمُ التَّيْمِيُّ لَمْ يَسْمَعْ مِنْ عَائِشَةَ ‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو دَاوُدَ مَاتَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ التَّيْمِيُّ وَلَمْ يَبْلُغْ أَرْبَعِينَ سَنَةً وَكَانَ يُكْنَى أَبَا أَسْمَاءَ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu\'minin: The Prophet (ﷺ) kissed me and did not perform ablution.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAbu Dawud said: This tradition is Mursal (i.e. where the link of the Companions is missing and the Successor reports from the Prophet directly). Ibrahim at-Taimi did not hear anything from \'Aishah.\\n\\n\\nAbu Dawud said: Al-Firyabi and other narrated this tradition in a like manner.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Purification (Kitab Al-Taharah)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3],\"ai_explanation\":\"The excerpt from Abudawud\'s Purification (Kitab Al-Taharah) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ) kissed Aisha without performing ablution. This tradition is considered Mursal, meaning the link between the Companion and the Successor is missing. The authenticity of this tradition is uncertain due to the limited information provided.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:59:02', '2026-03-02 01:59:02'),
(19, 'af9898ed50ee6818b03b59eaa6e5b84c80bafadd2548edd1f5fd405e9a53df0f', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:54\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ يَـٰقَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنفُسَكُم بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ فَتُوبُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰ بَارِئِكُمْ فَٱقْتُلُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَكُمْ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ عِندَ بَارِئِكُمْ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ ۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ\",\"english\":\"And [recall] when Moses said to his people, \\\"O my people, indeed you have wronged yourselves by your taking of the calf [for worship]. So repent to your Creator and kill yourselves. That is best for [all of] you in the sight of your Creator.\\\" Then He accepted your repentance; indeed, He is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:54\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"ai_explanation\":\"This excerpt from Surah 2:54 refers to a situation where Moses\' people were instructed to kill themselves as a form of repentance for worshiping the calf. The context suggests that this was a collective punishment and a means to atone for their wrongdoing. However, it\'s uncertain if this instruction applies to individual situations outside of this specific context.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 07:59:29', '2026-03-02 01:59:29'),
(20, 'c7c2fab13afbf736b3c4a4852dccb4ce9d6fa5ef5f3cc9fc375156fbf6f5fde7', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Battles (Kitab Al-Malahim)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا حَيْوَةُ بْنُ شُرَيْحٍ، حَدَّثَنَا بَقِيَّةُ، حَدَّثَنِي بَحِيرٌ، عَنْ خَالِدِ بْنِ مَعْدَانَ، عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ الأَسْوَدِ، عَنْ جُنَادَةَ بْنِ أَبِي أُمَيَّةَ، عَنْ عُبَادَةَ بْنِ الصَّامِتِ، أَنَّهُ حَدَّثَهُمْ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ ‏\\n\\\"‏ إِنِّي قَدْ حَدَّثْتُكُمْ عَنِ الدَّجَّالِ حَتَّى خَشِيتُ أَنْ لاَ تَعْقِلُوا إِنَّ مَسِيحَ الدَّجَّالِ رَجُلٌ قَصِيرٌ أَفْحَجُ جَعْدٌ أَعْوَرُ مَطْمُوسُ الْعَيْنِ لَيْسَ بِنَاتِئَةٍ وَلاَ جَحْرَاءَ فَإِنْ أُلْبِسَ عَلَيْكُمْ فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ رَبَّكُمْ لَيْسَ بِأَعْوَرَ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو دَاوُدَ عَمْرُو بْنُ الأَسْوَدِ وَلِيَ الْقَضَاءَ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Ubadah ibn as-Samit: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: I have told you so much about the Dajjal (Antichrist) that I am afraid you may not understand. The Antichrist is short, hen-toed, woolly-haired, one-eyed, an eye-sightless, and neither protruding nor deep-seated. If you are confused about him, know that your Lord is not one-eyed.\\n\\n\\nAbu Dawud said: \'Amr bin Al-Aswad was appointed a judge.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Battles (Kitab Al-Malahim)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[11],\"ai_explanation\":\"The Dajjal (Antichrist) is described as a short, hen-toed, woolly-haired, one-eyed person with poor eyesight. He is neither protruding nor deep-seated. The Prophet (ﷺ) warned that if the Dajjal is disguised, one should know that their Lord is not one-eyed. This description is based on the available excerpt and may not be comprehensive due to its limited nature.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:01:13', '2026-03-02 02:01:13'),
(21, '9a240e9d5d5eafdfb9df8c937e4648708293b7a96c65337fc44e9cb8ca06c072', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:22\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"ٱلَّذِى جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ فِرَٰشًا وَٱلسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَأَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَأَخْرَجَ بِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۖ فَلَا تَجْعَلُوا۟ لِلَّهِ أَندَادًا وَأَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\",\"english\":\"[He] who made for you the earth a bed [spread out] and the sky a ceiling and sent down from the sky, rain and brought forth thereby fruits as provision for you. So do not attribute to Allah equals while you know [that there is nothing similar to Him].\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:22\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the provided excerpt (Surah 2:22), Firaun (Pharaoh) is not directly mentioned. However, the verse describes Allah\'s creation and provision for humans, contrasting it with attributing equals to Allah. Since Firaun is not mentioned in this excerpt, I must rely on other sources for information about Firaun. However, based on the context of the Quran, Firaun is often associated with the story of Prophet Musa (Moses) and his people in Egypt. This excerpt does not provide information about Firaun.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:02:36', '2026-03-02 02:02:36'),
(22, '2804fc371bcbb83b741243dabf614158f457545b5eeda24d1725e5f9c1545d94', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:22\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"ٱلَّذِى جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ فِرَٰشًا وَٱلسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَأَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَأَخْرَجَ بِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۖ فَلَا تَجْعَلُوا۟ لِلَّهِ أَندَادًا وَأَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\",\"english\":\"[He] who made for you the earth a bed [spread out] and the sky a ceiling and sent down from the sky, rain and brought forth thereby fruits as provision for you. So do not attribute to Allah equals while you know [that there is nothing similar to Him].\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:22\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"From the provided excerpt (Surah 2:22), Pharaoh is not mentioned directly. However, the verse describes Allah\'s creation and provision for humans, including making the earth a bed and the sky a ceiling, and sending down rain to bring forth fruits as provision. This excerpt does not provide information about Pharaoh.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:03:27', '2026-03-02 02:03:27'),
(23, 'c71b758c692e871e6e1c0d858febe0ce2b6a8e50bb1adf6e63fd20ddbc4157e6', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:238\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَـٰفِظُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلصَّلَوَٰتِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱلْوُسْطَىٰ وَقُومُوا۟ لِلَّهِ قَـٰنِتِينَ\",\"english\":\"Maintain with care the [obligatory] prayers and [in particular] the middle prayer and stand before Allah, devoutly obedient.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:238\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[12],\"ai_explanation\":\"To give a prayer before sleep, we can refer to the excerpt from Surah 2:238. However, it does not directly mention a prayer for sleep. The excerpt emphasizes maintaining care for obligatory prayers, particularly the middle prayer, and standing before Allah in devotion. If we consider the broader context of prayer and devotion, a possible prayer before sleep could be: \\\"Oh Allah, I submit to You and stand before You in devotion. Guide me through the night and protect me from harm. I seek Your forgiveness and mercy. In Your name, I sleep and wake.\\\"\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:03:55', '2026-03-02 02:03:55'),
(24, '372f47deda38bf9e34b5abf7dd5f47c3db3069761f31b93a0e8f6564bb6d38d8', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #100\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #99\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"﴿اللَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ لاَ تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلاَ نَوْمٌ لَّهُ مَا فِي السَّمَوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الأَرْضِ مَن ذَا الَّذِي يَشْفَعُ عِنْـــــــــــدَهُ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَلاَ يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيْءٍ مِّنْ عِلْمِهِ إِلاَّ بِمَا شَاء وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضَ وَلاَ يَؤُودُهُ حِفْظُهُمَا وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيمُ﴾.\",\"english\":\"Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of [all] existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Who is it that can intercede with Him except by His permission? He knows what is [presently] before them and what will be after them, and they encompass not a thing of His knowledge except for what He wills. His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth, and their preservation tires Him not. And He is the Most High, the Most Great.\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #100\",\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"arabic\":\"((يَجْمَعُ كَفَّيْهِ ثُمَّ يَنْفُثُ فِيهِمَا فَيَقْرَأُ فِيهِمَا:بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ * اللَّهُ الصَّمَدُ* لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ* وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُ كُفُواً أَحَدٌ﴾.  بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ* مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ* وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ* وَمِن شَرِّ النَّفَّاثَاتِ فِي الْعُقَدِ* وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ﴾.  بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ* مَلِكِ النَّاسِ* إِلَهِ النَّاسِ* مِن شَرِّ الْوَسْوَاسِ الْخَنَّاسِ* الَّذِي يُوَسْوِسُ فِي صُدُورِ النَّاسِ* مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَ النَّاسِ﴾ ثُمَّ يَمْسَحُ بِهِمَا مَا اسْتَطَاعَ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ يَبْدَأُ بِهِمَا عَلَى رَأْسِهِ وَوَجْهِهِ وَمَا أَقبَلَ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ)) (يفعلُ ذلك ثلاثَ مرَّاتٍ).\",\"english\":\"(When retiring to his bed every night, the Prophet  would hold his palms together, spit (A form of spitting comprising mainly of air with little spittle) in them, recite the last three chapters (Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq, An-Nas) of the Quran and then wipe over his entire body as much as possible with his hands, beginning with his head and face and then all parts of the body, he would do this three times.)\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #99\",\"type\":\"dua\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3,2],\"ai_explanation\":\"To make dua before sleep, you can recite the following: 1. From excerpt #1: Recite the verse (Al-Baqarah 2:255) which describes Allah\'s attributes, such as being the Ever-Living and Sustainer of existence. 2. From excerpt #2: Recite the last three chapters of the Quran (Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq, and An-Nas) as the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to do before sleep. It is recommended to recite these duas before sleep, but the exact method is not specified in the provided excerpts.\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:04:40', '2026-03-02 02:04:40'),
(25, 'f38e114be047cf84e21518cd2abf25b4b12e290c7941c9e5d60b51456f7144db', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Jihad (Kitab Al-Jihad)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ أَبِي شَيْبَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ إِدْرِيسَ، عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ إِسْحَاقَ، عَنْ إِسْمَاعِيلَ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ، عَنْ أَبِي الزُّبَيْرِ، عَنْ سَعِيدِ بْنِ جُبَيْرٍ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏:‏ ‏\\\"‏ لَمَّا أُصِيبَ إِخْوَانُكُمْ بِأُحُدٍ جَعَلَ اللَّهُ أَرْوَاحَهُمْ فِي جَوْفِ طَيْرٍ خُضْرٍ تَرِدُ أَنْهَارَ الْجَنَّةِ، تَأْكُلُ مِنْ ثِمَارِهَا، وَتَأْوِي إِلَى قَنَادِيلَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ مُعَلَّقَةٍ فِي ظِلِّ الْعَرْشِ، فَلَمَّا وَجَدُوا طِيبَ مَأْكَلِهِمْ وَمَشْرَبِهِمْ وَمَقِيلِهِمْ قَالُوا ‏:‏ مَنْ يُبَلِّغُ إِخْوَانَنَا عَنَّا أَنَّا أَحْيَاءٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ نُرْزَقُ لِئَلاَّ يَزْهَدُوا فِي الْجِهَادِ وَلاَ يَنْكُلُوا عِنْدَ الْحَرْبِ فَقَالَ اللَّهُ سُبْحَانَهُ ‏:‏ أَنَا أُبَلِّغُهُمْ عَنْكُمْ ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏:‏ فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ ‏{‏ وَلاَ تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَاتًا ‏}‏ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏ إِلَى آخِرِ الآيَةِ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: When your brethren were smitten at the battle of Uhud, Allah put their spirits in the crops of green birds which go down to the rivers of Paradise, eat its fruit and nestle in lamps of gold in the shade of the Throne. Then when they experienced the sweetness of their food, drink and rest, they asked: Who will tell our brethren about us that we are alive in Paradise provided with provision, in order that they might not be disinterested in jihad and recoil in war? Allah Most High said: I shall tell them about you; so Allah sent down; \\\"And do not consider those who have been killed in Allah\'s path.\\\" till the end of the verse.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Jihad (Kitab Al-Jihad)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[16],\"ai_explanation\":\"The hadith mentions that when the companions were killed at the Battle of Uhud, Allah placed their spirits in green birds that lived in Paradise. These birds experienced the sweetness of their food, drink, and rest, and asked Allah to inform their brethren about their fate. Allah agreed and sent down a verse to reassure the companions that those who died in His path are not dead, as mentioned in the verse: \\\"And do not consider those who have been killed in Allah\'s path.\\\"\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:06:04', '2026-03-02 02:06:04'),
(26, 'fba7f99ee038873b3ac0fe41d87438575942fcf974e170c3c3273c65e98f9d5a', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 3:121\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِذْ غَدَوْتَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ تُبَوِّئُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ مَقَـٰعِدَ لِلْقِتَالِ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"And [remember] when you, [O Muhammad], left your family in the morning to post the believers at their stations for the battle [of Uhud] - and Allah is Hearing and Knowing -\",\"reference\":\"Surah 3:121\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"This aya (verse) refers to the Battle of Uhud. It mentions the Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) leaving his family to position the believers for the battle. The aya highlights Allah\'s knowledge and hearing of this event. (Note: The excerpt is limited to this specific event, so further context may be required for a more detailed explanation.)\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 08:06:50', '2026-03-02 02:06:50'),
(27, '9cf63fbf55ba3fb41eba74f383259b4156b8885f5ffbbb26f278dfd5fb7a631e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 8:5\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"كَمَآ أَخْرَجَكَ رَبُّكَ مِنۢ بَيْتِكَ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَإِنَّ فَرِيقًا مِّنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ لَكَـٰرِهُونَ\",\"english\":\"[It is] just as when your Lord brought you out of your home [for the battle of Badr] in truth, while indeed, a party among the believers were unwilling,\",\"reference\":\"Surah 8:5\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3],\"ai_explanation\":\"The battle of Badr took place when the believers were brought out of their home by their Lord in truth. This information is based on Surah 8:5, which mentions the event of the believers being brought out of their home for the battle of Badr. However, the exact date is not specified in this excerpt.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:03:29', '2026-03-02 06:03:29'),
(28, '626367c9989e9b1a8891bedc39f25a7a133de863d9c72e1f191610a384c864d6', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:30\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَـٰٓئِكَةِ إِنِّى جَاعِلٌ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً ۖ قَالُوٓا۟ أَتَجْعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفْسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسْفِكُ ٱلدِّمَآءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ ۖ قَالَ إِنِّىٓ أَعْلَمُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ\",\"english\":\"And [mention, O Muhammad], when your Lord said to the angels, \\\"Indeed, I will make upon the earth a successive authority.\\\" They said, \\\"Will You place upon it one who causes corruption therein and sheds blood, while we declare Your praise and sanctify You?\\\" Allah said, \\\"Indeed, I know that which you do not know.\\\"\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:30\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2],\"ai_explanation\":\"This event is mentioned in Surah 2:30. However, the excerpt does not specify when the event took place. It only mentions a conversation between Allah and the angels about creating a \\\"successive authority\\\" on earth. Since the excerpt does not provide a clear timeline, we cannot determine the exact date or period when this event occurred.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:04:40', '2026-03-02 06:04:40'),
(29, '5896dc6f79c07b962a85bc2ee2fce56030c634fac4d33a9c2095fc8c5447af11', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"personal_verdict\",\"intent\":\"personal_verdict_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"type\":\"fatwa\",\"storage_type\":\"txt\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":5,\"dataset_name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"fatwa\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_18753 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"english\":\"Praise be to Allah.If you were certain that your menses had ended and you formed the intention to fast before dawn, even if it was one minute before, then your fast is valid, even if you delayed doing ghusl .  But if you were uncertain as to whether your period had ended, but you still intended to fast, then the fast was not valid because of your uncertainty as to whether your menses had ended.   Shaykh Ibn ‘Uthaymin (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about a woman who fasted when she was unsure whether her period was over, then when morning came she saw that it had indeed ended. Does her fast count even though she was not certain that her period had ended?  He replied:  “Her fast does not count, and she has to make up that day , because the basic principle is that the menses was still there, and her starting to fast when she was not certain that her menses was over means that she started to do an act of worship when she was uncertain as to whether one of the conditions of it being valid was fulfilled or not, and this means that it does not count.” (Majmu’ Fatawa al-Shaykh Ibn ‘Uthaymin, 19/107)                                                                                        If a woman knows that her menses has ended , she must do ghusl so that she may pray, and it is not permissible for her to delay that until the time for prayer ends. If she does that, then she has to repent, as well as make up the prayers that she has missed.  If she forgets that her period has ended – as you mention in your question – then there is no sin on her in sha Allah for delaying her prayer, but when she remembers she must do ghusl and offer the prayers that she has missed – as you did.  We ask Allah to forgive us and you.  And Allah knows best.\",\"text\":\"Question: Question  My menses ended before Fajr prayer and I waited until after the prayer, but I fell asleep and I woke up at ten a.m. I did not do ghusl because I forgot, and I took my sick daughter to the hospital, and I was busy until the time of ‘Asr prayer, then I did ghusl and made up the prayers that I had missed. Allah knows that this is the first time this had happened to me since I reached puberty. The reason was that my period usually lasts for 9 days but this month it was 8 days, but I waited to make sure, but I was fasting. What should I do? Should I make up the fast?\\n\\nAnswer: Praise be to Allah.If you were certain that your menses had ended and you formed the intention to fast before dawn, even if it was one minute before, then your fast is valid, even if you delayed doing ghusl .  But if you were uncertain as to whether your period had ended, but you still intended to fast, then the fast was not valid because of your uncertainty as to whether your menses had ended.   Shaykh Ibn ‘Uthaymin (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about a woman who fasted when she was unsure whether her period was over, then when morning came she saw that it had indeed ended. Does her fast count even though she was not certain that her period had ended?  He replied:  “Her fast does not count, and she has to make up that day , because the basic principle is that the menses was still there, and her starting to fast when she was not certain that her menses was over means that she started to do an act of worship when she was uncertain as to whether one of the conditions of it being valid was fulfilled or not, and this means that it does not count.” (Majmu’ Fatawa al-Shaykh Ibn ‘Uthaymin, 19/107)                                                                                        If a woman knows that her menses has ended , she must do ghusl so that she may pray, and it is not permissible for her to delay that until the time for prayer ends. If she does that, then she has to repent, as well as make up the prayers that she has missed.  If she forgets that her period has ended – as you mention in your question – then there is no sin on her in sha Allah for delaying her prayer, but when she remembers she must do ghusl and offer the prayers that she has missed – as you did.  We ask Allah to forgive us and you.  And Allah knows best.\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_18753 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\",\"type\":\"txt_qa\",\"question\":\"Question  My menses ended before Fajr prayer and I waited until after the prayer, but I fell asleep and I woke up at ten a.m. I did not do ghusl because I forgot, and I took my sick daughter to the hospital, and I was busy until the time of ‘Asr prayer, then I did ghusl and made up the prayers that I had missed. Allah knows that this is the first time this had happened to me since I reached puberty. The reason was that my period usually lasts for 9 days but this month it was 8 days, but I waited to make sure, but I was fasting. What should I do? Should I make up the fast?\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[12],\"ai_explanation\":\"If you were certain that your menses had ended and formed the intention to fast before dawn, your fast is valid even if you delayed doing ghusl. However, if you were uncertain about the end of your period, your fast is not valid. In your case, since you forgot to do ghusl before Maghrib, it is uncertain whether your fast is valid or not. Consult a scholar for a definitive ruling.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:06:43', '2026-03-02 06:06:43');
INSERT INTO `ai_cache` (`id`, `cache_key`, `response_json`, `expires_at`, `created_at`) VALUES
(30, 'e3b5f1167f0cbb1735d37651ac878e25ed5575ff126bf395d937387177fff42f', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"fiqh_explanation\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"type\":\"fatwa\",\"storage_type\":\"txt\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":5,\"dataset_name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"fatwa\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_26 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"english\":\"Praise be to Allah.Going to practitioners of magic, soothsayers and fortune-tellers is a major sin, because the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever goes to a fortune-teller and asks him about something, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights.” Narrated by Muslim, 2230.  And he (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in that which was revealed to Muhammad (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him).”  The one who goes to a fortune teller or practitioner of magic and believes his claim to have knowledge of the unseen has gone out of Islam.  But if he goes to him but does not believe his claim to have knowledge of the unseen, then he has committed a major sin but he has not gone out of Islam by doing that.  If the man was ignorant and did not realise that going to practitioners of magic is haraam, then we hope that this is an excuse for him before Allah, may He be exalted. So there are no consequences for his going to them and he has not gone out of Islam by doing that.  But in the case of one who goes to a practitioner of magic knowing that that is haraam, this is the one who has committed a major sin that may reach the level of going out of Islam.  See also the answer to questions no. 112069 and 32863.  Secondly:  The ruling that the one who does not pray out of laziness becomes a kaafir is the subject of a great difference of opinion among the scholars and each point of view has evidence on which it relies. The fatwa adopted by this website suggests the most likely opinion to be correct is that which says that the one who does not pray is a kaafir; this is the view of many scholars.  This has been discussed previously in the answers to questions no.  10094 and 5208.  Who has blessed your husband and guided him to start praying and to pray regularly.  Thirdly:  If a man says concerning his wife, “she is finished from me and me from her”, this is a phrase that may be understood as referring to divorce or it may not. Hence it cannot be deemed to count as a divorce unless the husband aimed thereby to divorce her and that was his intention; if he did not intend to divorce her and did not aim to do that, then no divorce has taken place.  See also the answer to questions 98670, 85575 and 127280.  As your husband has come to his senses and has started to pray regularly and has repented from going to practitioners of magic in addition to the fact that he was unaware of the shar‘i ruling at that time, what you have to do is to turn over a new leaf with him. And we ask Allah to bestow His mercy upon you and to reconcile between your hearts and bring you back together.  And Allah knows best.\",\"text\":\"Question: Question  My mother emotionally blackmailed me into marrying my first cousin 9 years ago when I was just 15 years old. i kept quiet out of fear and since then have been blessd with 3 beautifil boys alhamdulillaah. Since the last 2 years we have been problems and he went to see someone who plays with magic. As far as my limited knowledge is concerned that takes one out of the fold of islam. Also for a while he was neglecting his prayers and would only d pray sometimes anod do his jumah. But he has rpented since and prays 5 times a day alhamdulillaah. HE also said he didnt know what he was doin with regards to the magic as he was not in the right state of mindbut i dont know what to think as he said he diddnt know it was wrong amd kufr as he thought it would get us out of a difficult situation. He possesses no knowledge with regards to deen so my questions are: 1. Did the magic take him out of islam??, is it the same ruling for one who knows that its wrong and one who doesnt ?. 2. Also did the fact he neglected some of his prayers take him out of islambecause said he repented and started praying agai.n. 3.Also he left the house 3 months ago and before he left he said to my mum she is finished from me and me from her\' does tha count as a talaq? As he wa angry and left the house. He is currently abroad and hasnt really provided for the kids or me. H left all our debts to me but he said he will contribute once i let him back in but i dont know what to do. i love my kids and would do anything for them. I hope you can assist me in this matter soon as this has affected me and especiallymy 3 children who are all under the age of 8. It has left them distrssed and they want him back in the house. He has gone abroad for now and will be back iwthin a few weeks and i need this matter resolved soon inshaAllaah.\\n\\nAnswer: Praise be to Allah.Going to practitioners of magic, soothsayers and fortune-tellers is a major sin, because the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever goes to a fortune-teller and asks him about something, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights.” Narrated by Muslim, 2230.  And he (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in that which was revealed to Muhammad (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him).”  The one who goes to a fortune teller or practitioner of magic and believes his claim to have knowledge of the unseen has gone out of Islam.  But if he goes to him but does not believe his claim to have knowledge of the unseen, then he has committed a major sin but he has not gone out of Islam by doing that.  If the man was ignorant and did not realise that going to practitioners of magic is haraam, then we hope that this is an excuse for him before Allah, may He be exalted. So there are no consequences for his going to them and he has not gone out of Islam by doing that.  But in the case of one who goes to a practitioner of magic knowing that that is haraam, this is the one who has committed a major sin that may reach the level of going out of Islam.  See also the answer to questions no. 112069 and 32863.  Secondly:  The ruling that the one who does not pray out of laziness becomes a kaafir is the subject of a great difference of opinion among the scholars and each point of view has evidence on which it relies. The fatwa adopted by this website suggests the most likely opinion to be correct is that which says that the one who does not pray is a kaafir; this is the view of many scholars.  This has been discussed previously in the answers to questions no.  10094 and 5208.  Who has blessed your husband and guided him to start praying and to pray regularly.  Thirdly:  If a man says concerning his wife, “she is finished from me and me from her”, this is a phrase that may be understood as referring to divorce or it may not. Hence it cannot be deemed to count as a divorce unless the husband aimed thereby to divorce her and that was his intention; if he did not intend to divorce her and did not aim to do that, then no divorce has taken place.  See also the answer to questions 98670, 85575 and 127280.  As your husband has come to his senses and has started to pray regularly and has repented from going to practitioners of magic in addition to the fact that he was unaware of the shar‘i ruling at that time, what you have to do is to turn over a new leaf with him. And we ask Allah to bestow His mercy upon you and to reconcile between your hearts and bring you back together.  And Allah knows best.\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_26 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\",\"type\":\"txt_qa\",\"question\":\"Question  My mother emotionally blackmailed me into marrying my first cousin 9 years ago when I was just 15 years old. i kept quiet out of fear and since then have been blessd with 3 beautifil boys alhamdulillaah. Since the last 2 years we have been problems and he went to see someone who plays with magic. As far as my limited knowledge is concerned that takes one out of the fold of islam. Also for a while he was neglecting his prayers and would only d pray sometimes anod do his jumah. But he has rpented since and prays 5 times a day alhamdulillaah. HE also said he didnt know what he was doin with regards to the magic as he was not in the right state of mindbut i dont know what to think as he said he diddnt know it was wrong amd kufr as he thought it would get us out of a difficult situation. He possesses no knowledge with regards to deen so my questions are: 1. Did the magic take him out of islam??, is it the same ruling for one who knows that its wrong and one who doesnt ?. 2. Also did the fact he neglected some of his prayers take him out of islambecause said he repented and started praying agai.n. 3.Also he left the house 3 months ago and before he left he said to my mum she is finished from me and me from her\' does tha count as a talaq? As he wa angry and left the house. He is currently abroad and hasnt really provided for the kids or me. H left all our debts to me but he said he will contribute once i let him back in but i dont know what to do. i love my kids and would do anything for them. I hope you can assist me in this matter soon as this has affected me and especiallymy 3 children who are all under the age of 8. It has left them distrssed and they want him back in the house. He has gone abroad for now and will be back iwthin a few weeks and i need this matter resolved soon inshaAllaah.\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"ai_explanation\":\"The ruling on someone who does not pray out of laziness is a subject of difference of opinion among scholars. The fatwa adopted by this website suggests that the one who does not pray is a kaafir, which is the view of many scholars. However, this is based on limited knowledge and the excerpt does not provide a clear answer. It is mentioned that if someone neglects prayer due to ignorance, it may be an excuse before Allah. But if someone knows it is wrong and still does not pray, it may be considered a major sin that could lead to going out of Islam.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:11:34', '2026-03-02 06:11:34'),
(31, '16761a35699e551972413d88cb5efc9d17460fd68087a2e7b9c9157e28d764b3', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:238\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَـٰفِظُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلصَّلَوَٰتِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱلْوُسْطَىٰ وَقُومُوا۟ لِلَّهِ قَـٰنِتِينَ\",\"english\":\"Maintain with care the [obligatory] prayers and [in particular] the middle prayer and stand before Allah, devoutly obedient.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:238\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[13],\"ai_explanation\":\"Based on the excerpt from Surah 2:238, to advise someone who sometimes leaves prayer, you can remind them to: \\\"Maintain with care the [obligatory] prayers and [in particular] the middle prayer.\\\" (Surah 2:238) This verse emphasizes the importance of being regular and diligent in performing prayers. You can encourage them to be more mindful and consistent in their prayer routine.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:13:17', '2026-03-02 06:13:17'),
(32, '1130ec2bf25232f093373a7723c92d581647857a8eccedab70e01dec9764e09e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"personal_verdict\",\"intent\":\"personal_verdict_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"type\":\"fatwa\",\"storage_type\":\"txt\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":5,\"dataset_name\":\"IslamQA English TXT Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"fatwa\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_14551 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"english\":\"Praise be to Allah.Firstly: The opening takbir (takbirat al-ihram) is one of the essential parts of the prayer The opening takbir (takbirat al-ihram) is one of the essential parts of the prayer; it is not waived if one forgets it or is unaware of the ruling, and nothing else can take its place. If a person remembers during his prayer that he forgot to say the opening takbir, or he is not sure whether he did it, he must start his prayer all over again, as we explained previously in the answer to question no. 69853 . As for being uncertain as to whether you pronounced it correctly or not, if that stems from waswasah (intrusive thoughts or whispers from the Shaytan), then you should ignore it and not pay any attention to it. Secondly: Repeating the opening takbir The one who repeats the opening takbir has invalidated his first prayer, and the ones who are praying behind him have now preceded him in saying the opening takbir with regard to his second prayer, in which they followed him. But this preceding of the imam may be overlooked, because there is a valid reason for it, as some of the scholars pointed out Al-Bujayrami said in his commentary on al-Khatib (2/14): The words “if the worshipper delayed his opening takbir until after the imam [had said it]” refer to the entire takbir. If his takbir partially overlaps with that of the imam, then his following of the imam in prayer is not valid, and he is not regarded as having begun the prayer except in two scenarios in which it is permissible for the one who is praying behind the imam to say the opening takbir before the imam: [The first scenario is] if he said the opening takbir on his own, then joined a congregation after that. The second scenario is if the imam and the people behind him said the opening takbir, then the imam was not sure of his own intention, so he repeated the takbir with the intention of starting the prayer, saying it in such a way that only he himself could hear it, and he continued to lead the prayer. End quote. Al-Jamal (may Allah have mercy on him) said in his commentary on Sharh al-Manhaj (1/567): az-Zarkashi said: al-Hannati was asked about a man who said the opening takbir for a prayer in which he was leading the people, then he repeated the takbir quietly to himself, and he did not make the people aware of that after they said the opening takbir themselves. He said: The prayer of the congregation is valid according to the more correct of the two scholarly views. End quote. The view of the Hanafis is more lenient than that. They think that he is still in a state of prayer, and that his second takbir does not interrupt his prayer and does not invalidate his first takbir. In al-Asl by Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ash-Shaybani, it says: What about a man who started to pray and recited Qur’an, then he became uncertain and was not sure whether he had said the opening takbir or not, so he repeated the opening takbir and the recitation, then he realised that he had said the takbir the first time? He said: He should continue his prayer, and he must do the two prostrations of forgetfulness. I said: Doesn’t this takbir interrupt his prayer? He said no; do you not see that his intention is only to do the same prayer, and he does not intend any other prayer. \\\"(al-Asl 1/226). The hadith of Sahl ibn Sa‘d as-Sa‘idi may be quoted as evidence for it being permissible for the one who is praying behind an imam to say the opening takbir before his imam in such exceptional circumstances. This hadith says that the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) went to Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf to resolve a dispute among them. The time for prayer came, and the mu’adhdhin came to Abu Bakr and said: Will you lead the people in prayer, and I will say the iqaamah? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, then the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) came whilst the people were still praying. He came and stood in the row, and the people started clapping. Abu Bakr used not to pay attention to anything whilst he was praying, but when the people’s clapping increased, he turned around and saw the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to stay where he was. Abu Bakr raised his hands and praised Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, for the command of the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him). Then Abu Bakr moved backwards until he was level with the row, and the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) came forward and led the prayer … Narrated by al-Bukhari (684) and Muslim (42`). Conclusion: The prayer of the congregation is valid, and nothing is required of you or them. But what you must do is ignore waswas (intrusive thoughts or whispers from the Shaytan) and not pay attention to it, because it could invalidate a person’s prayer and, moreover, cause him a great deal of trouble. And Allah knows best.\",\"text\":\"Question: Question  I was an imam, leading the people in prayer. After I had said the opening takbir, I was not sure whether I had said it properly, so I quietly repeated it, and the people praying behind me were not aware of that. We completed the prayer on that basis, with the intention that I was their imam who was leading them in prayer. Is their prayer invalid, and do I have to bring them together and tell them about that? This is something that I am not able to do, because I do not know them all.\\n\\nAnswer: Praise be to Allah.Firstly: The opening takbir (takbirat al-ihram) is one of the essential parts of the prayer The opening takbir (takbirat al-ihram) is one of the essential parts of the prayer; it is not waived if one forgets it or is unaware of the ruling, and nothing else can take its place. If a person remembers during his prayer that he forgot to say the opening takbir, or he is not sure whether he did it, he must start his prayer all over again, as we explained previously in the answer to question no. 69853 . As for being uncertain as to whether you pronounced it correctly or not, if that stems from waswasah (intrusive thoughts or whispers from the Shaytan), then you should ignore it and not pay any attention to it. Secondly: Repeating the opening takbir The one who repeats the opening takbir has invalidated his first prayer, and the ones who are praying behind him have now preceded him in saying the opening takbir with regard to his second prayer, in which they followed him. But this preceding of the imam may be overlooked, because there is a valid reason for it, as some of the scholars pointed out Al-Bujayrami said in his commentary on al-Khatib (2/14): The words “if the worshipper delayed his opening takbir until after the imam [had said it]” refer to the entire takbir. If his takbir partially overlaps with that of the imam, then his following of the imam in prayer is not valid, and he is not regarded as having begun the prayer except in two scenarios in which it is permissible for the one who is praying behind the imam to say the opening takbir before the imam: [The first scenario is] if he said the opening takbir on his own, then joined a congregation after that. The second scenario is if the imam and the people behind him said the opening takbir, then the imam was not sure of his own intention, so he repeated the takbir with the intention of starting the prayer, saying it in such a way that only he himself could hear it, and he continued to lead the prayer. End quote. Al-Jamal (may Allah have mercy on him) said in his commentary on Sharh al-Manhaj (1/567): az-Zarkashi said: al-Hannati was asked about a man who said the opening takbir for a prayer in which he was leading the people, then he repeated the takbir quietly to himself, and he did not make the people aware of that after they said the opening takbir themselves. He said: The prayer of the congregation is valid according to the more correct of the two scholarly views. End quote. The view of the Hanafis is more lenient than that. They think that he is still in a state of prayer, and that his second takbir does not interrupt his prayer and does not invalidate his first takbir. In al-Asl by Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ash-Shaybani, it says: What about a man who started to pray and recited Qur’an, then he became uncertain and was not sure whether he had said the opening takbir or not, so he repeated the opening takbir and the recitation, then he realised that he had said the takbir the first time? He said: He should continue his prayer, and he must do the two prostrations of forgetfulness. I said: Doesn’t this takbir interrupt his prayer? He said no; do you not see that his intention is only to do the same prayer, and he does not intend any other prayer. \\\"(al-Asl 1/226). The hadith of Sahl ibn Sa‘d as-Sa‘idi may be quoted as evidence for it being permissible for the one who is praying behind an imam to say the opening takbir before his imam in such exceptional circumstances. This hadith says that the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) went to Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf to resolve a dispute among them. The time for prayer came, and the mu’adhdhin came to Abu Bakr and said: Will you lead the people in prayer, and I will say the iqaamah? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, then the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) came whilst the people were still praying. He came and stood in the row, and the people started clapping. Abu Bakr used not to pay attention to anything whilst he was praying, but when the people’s clapping increased, he turned around and saw the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to stay where he was. Abu Bakr raised his hands and praised Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, for the command of the Messenger of Allah (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him). Then Abu Bakr moved backwards until he was level with the row, and the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) came forward and led the prayer … Narrated by al-Bukhari (684) and Muslim (42`). Conclusion: The prayer of the congregation is valid, and nothing is required of you or them. But what you must do is ignore waswas (intrusive thoughts or whispers from the Shaytan) and not pay attention to it, because it could invalidate a person’s prayer and, moreover, cause him a great deal of trouble. And Allah knows best.\",\"reference\":\"IslamQA islamqa_14551 (kingkaung/english_islamqainfo)\",\"type\":\"txt_qa\",\"question\":\"Question  I was an imam, leading the people in prayer. After I had said the opening takbir, I was not sure whether I had said it properly, so I quietly repeated it, and the people praying behind me were not aware of that. We completed the prayer on that basis, with the intention that I was their imam who was leading them in prayer. Is their prayer invalid, and do I have to bring them together and tell them about that? This is something that I am not able to do, because I do not know them all.\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3],\"ai_explanation\":\"If you delayed your prayer, the validity depends on the circumstances. If you were unsure about the opening takbir and repeated it quietly, the prayer of the congregation is valid according to some scholars. However, if you partially overlapped with the imam\'s takbir, your following of the imam in prayer is not valid. It is recommended to ignore waswas (intrusive thoughts or whispers from the Shaytan) and not pay attention to it, as it could invalidate a person\'s prayer. Consult verified scholars for a definitive ruling.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:15:40', '2026-03-02 06:15:40'),
(33, '67b5de8e77e94b2431a2e14cec225ab1f5229b435e489d7c4f38991d420395d9', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Ar Raheem\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Ar Rahmaan\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الرَّحِيمُ\",\"english\":\"Ar Raheem - The Most Compassionate. The One who has plenty of mercy for the believers.\",\"reference\":\"Ar Raheem\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"},{\"arabic\":\"الرَّحْمَنُ\",\"english\":\"Ar Rahmaan - The Most Merciful. The One who has plenty of mercy for the believers and the blasphemers in this world and especially for the believers in the hereafter.\",\"reference\":\"Ar Rahmaan\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2,1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Two names of Allah associated with mercy are: 1. Ar Raheem (Arabic: الرَّحِيمُ) - The Most Compassionate, having plenty of mercy for believers. 2. Ar Rahmaan (Arabic: الرَّحْمَنُ) - The Most Merciful, having plenty of mercy for both believers and blasphemers, especially believers in the hereafter. Note: The excerpts provide a general understanding, but the full scope of these names may be more extensive.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:54:33', '2026-03-02 06:54:33'),
(34, '41aae82bd35571eeb60f4c1f98975833410dff40fda2ebb42962f376fe0bd0d7', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghafoor\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Afuww\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفَّارُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"},{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفُورُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghafoor - The Great Forgiver. The One who forgives a lot.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghafoor\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"},{\"arabic\":\"العَفُوُّ\",\"english\":\"Al Afuww - The Pardoner. The One with wide forgiveness.\",\"reference\":\"Al Afuww\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1,5,9],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Here are 3 names of Allah with explanations: 1. Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. Forgives the sins of His slaves repeatedly. 2. Al Ghafoor - The Great Forgiver. Forgives a lot. 3. Al Afuww - The Pardoner. Has wide forgiveness. Note: These explanations are based on the provided dataset excerpts and may not be exhaustive.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:55:30', '2026-03-02 06:55:30'),
(35, '4a823ad69b30ca7134b5b758e9afdd7b4bb5be2d84ae12f4caaa9484dc7f3ec2', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghafoor\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفُورُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghafoor - The Great Forgiver. The One who forgives a lot.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghafoor\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"},{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفَّارُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[5,1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Here are 3 random names of Allah from the dataset: 1. Al Ghafoor - The Great Forgiver. The One who forgives a lot. 2. Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again. 3. (Limited excerpt, uncertain) Al Ghaffaar is mentioned, but another name is Al Kareem (not in the provided excerpts). Follow-up: 4. Al Kareem (not in the provided excerpts, but mentioned as a possible name) 5. Al Hakeem (not in the provided excerpts)\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:55:43', '2026-03-02 06:55:43'),
