(37, 'a9360699e8acced0ccfb2a6861c8995388810ce88d5f8d57d17c03ae1db98cdc', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #56\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عَذَابِ الْقَبْرِ، وَأَعوذُ بِكَ مِنْ فِتْنَةِ الْمَسِيحِ الدَّجَّالِ، وَأَعوذُ بِكَ مِنْ فِتْنَةِ الْمَحْيَا وَالْمَمَاتِ. اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْمَأْثَمِ وَالْمَغْرَمِ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, I take refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I take refuge in You from the temptation and trial of Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal, and I take refuge in You from the trials and tribulations of life and death.  O Allah, I take refuge in You from sin and debt.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #56\",\"type\":\"dua\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[15],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Before going out, a common supplication is: (O Allah, I take refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I take refuge in You from the temptation and trial of Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal, and I take refuge in You from the trials and tribulations of life and death. O Allah, I take refuge in You from sin and debt.) This is excerpt #56, Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer.\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:56:38', '2026-03-02 06:56:38'),
(38, 'a28a9c8f7a849c3fa491d7f4edf2aa268aaaf81bad243fe0fe65eb5a69c93861', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا أَحْمَدُ بْنُ مُحَمَّدٍ، حَدَّثَنِي عَلِيُّ بْنُ حُسَيْنٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ يَزِيدَ النَّحْوِيِّ، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، ‏{‏ وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ فِدْيَةٌ طَعَامُ مِسْكِينٍ ‏}‏ فَكَانَ مَنْ شَاءَ مِنْهُمْ أَنْ يَفْتَدِيَ بِطَعَامِ مِسْكِينٍ افْتَدَى وَتَمَّ لَهُ صَوْمُهُ فَقَالَ ‏{‏ فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَهُ وَأَنْ تَصُومُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ‏}‏ وَقَالَ ‏{‏ فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ وَمَنْ كَانَ مَرِيضًا أَوْ عَلَى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ ‏}‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Ibn ‘Abbas explain the Qur’anic verse “For those who can do it(with hardship) is a ransom, the feeding of one, that is indigent” said “If one of them wished to pay ransom by providing food to an indigent person he could pay ransom.. Thus, his fast was complete. Allaah, the Exalted pronounced “But he that will give more of his own free will, it is better for him”. Again he pronounced “So every one of you who is present (at his home) during that month should spend it in fasting.” But, if anyone is ill or on a journey the prescribed period (should be made up) by days later.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Ibn \'Abbas, those who find fasting difficult have the option to pay a ransom (fidyah) by feeding a poor person. If they choose to do so, their fast is considered complete. However, if they wish to give more, it is better for them. The verse also mentions that those who are present during Ramadan should fast, but if someone is ill or traveling, they can make up the missed days later. This explanation is based on the provided excerpt and might be limited in scope.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:57:40', '2026-03-02 06:57:40'),
(39, '9778497de7d27dab22d52df260ffa37a690a2c588df5ade93260d86f57cb6da9', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"hadith_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا نَصْرُ بْنُ عَلِيِّ بْنِ نَصْرٍ الْجَهْضَمِيُّ، أَخْبَرَنَا أَبُو أَحْمَدَ، أَخْبَرَنَا إِسْرَائِيلُ، عَنْ إِسْحَاقَ، عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ، قَالَ كَانَ الرَّجُلُ إِذَا صَامَ فَنَامَ لَمْ يَأْكُلْ إِلَى مِثْلِهَا وَإِنَّ صِرْمَةَ بْنَ قَيْسٍ الأَنْصَارِيَّ أَتَى امْرَأَتَهُ وَكَانَ صَائِمًا فَقَالَ عِنْدَكِ شَىْءٌ قَالَتْ لاَ لَعَلِّي أَذْهَبُ فَأَطْلُبُ لَكَ شَيْئًا ‏.‏ فَذَهَبَتْ وَغَلَبَتْهُ عَيْنُهُ فَجَاءَتْ فَقَالَتْ خَيْبَةً لَكَ ‏.‏ فَلَمْ يَنْتَصِفِ النَّهَارُ حَتَّى غُشِيَ عَلَيْهِ وَكَانَ يَعْمَلُ يَوْمَهُ فِي أَرْضِهِ فَذَكَرَ ذَلِكَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَنَزَلَتْ ‏{‏ أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيَامِ الرَّفَثُ إِلَى نِسَائِكُمْ ‏}‏ قَرَأَ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏ مِنَ الْفَجْرِ ‏}‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Al Bara’ (bin Azib) said “When a man fasted and slept, he could not eat till (another nigh) like it.” Sarmah bin Qais Al Ansari came to his wife while he was fasting and asked her Do you have something (to eat)? She replied “No”. Let me go and seek something for you. So, she went out and sleep overcame him. She came (back) and said (to him) .You are deprived (of food). He fainted before noon. He used to work all day long at his land. This was mentioned to the Prophet (ﷺ). So the following verse was revealed. “Permitted to you on the nights of the fasts, is the approach to your wives. They are your garments and ye are their garments. Allah knoweth what yes used to do secretly amongst yourselves. But he turned to you and forgave you. So now associate with them and seek what Allaah hath ordained for you. And eat and drink until the white thread of dawn appears to you. He recited up to the words “of dawn”.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\",\"type\":\"hadith\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Abudawud\'s Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam), when a man fasts and sleeps, he cannot eat till another similar period. This was mentioned to the Prophet (ﷺ), and as a result, the verse \\\"Permitted to you on the nights of the fasts, is the approach to your wives\\\" was revealed. This excerpt implies that fasting rewards include the ability to abstain from food and drink until dawn, but it does not explicitly state the reward. The relationship between fasting and the verse\'s revelation is mentioned, but the reward itself is not directly explained.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 12:58:21', '2026-03-02 06:58:21'),
(40, '613677739692fd04a550baa622224ee6145da7b6bb50651de0196a0d577cf8d5', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 5:33\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"إِنَّمَا جَزَٰٓؤُا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ فَسَادًا أَن يُقَتَّلُوٓا۟ أَوْ يُصَلَّبُوٓا۟ أَوْ تُقَطَّعَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَأَرْجُلُهُم مِّنْ خِلَـٰفٍ أَوْ يُنفَوْا۟ مِنَ ٱلْأَرْضِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لَهُمْ خِزْىٌ فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا ۖ وَلَهُمْ فِى ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"Indeed, the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive upon earth [to cause] corruption is none but that they be killed or crucified or that their hands and feet be cut off from opposite sides or that they be exiled from the land. That is for them a disgrace in this world; and for them in the Hereafter is a great punishment,\",\"reference\":\"Surah 5:33\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[5],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"The dataset excerpt does not explicitly mention the penalty for drinking alcohol. It describes the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive upon earth to cause corruption, which includes killing, crucifixion, cutting off hands and feet, or exile. This excerpt is limited in scope and does not address the specific topic of drinking alcohol. This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 13:01:49', '2026-03-02 07:01:49'),
(41, '1588e06841e79905b714683d60bcf8759bbf57112534d44c96fd064c50acaead', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:168\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ كُلُوا۟ مِمَّا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ حَلَـٰلًا طَيِّبًا وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوا۟ خُطُوَٰتِ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِينٌ\",\"english\":\"O mankind, eat from whatever is on earth [that is] lawful and good and do not follow the footsteps of Satan. Indeed, he is to you a clear enemy.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:168\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[12],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Surah 2:168, the penalty for drinking alcohol is not explicitly mentioned. However, it advises to \\\"eat from whatever is on earth [that is] lawful and good\\\" and warns against following Satan, implying that alcohol is considered haram (forbidden). The excerpt does not provide a specific penalty, indicating uncertainty due to its limited scope.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 13:02:14', '2026-03-02 07:02:14'),
(42, 'bc4462fed4c6620e85849d6d777d939bfd9af600d48f5c4c982f16d2eda365b5', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:112\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"بَلَىٰ مَنْ أَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ فَلَهُۥٓ أَجْرُهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ\",\"english\":\"Yes [on the contrary], whoever submits his face in Islam to Allah while being a doer of good will have his reward with his Lord. And no fear will there be concerning them, nor will they grieve.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:112\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[6],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"In Islam, alcohol is considered haram (forbidden). However, the provided excerpt does not directly mention alcohol. It discusses the reward of those who submit to Allah and do good deeds (Surah 2:112). This excerpt does not provide information about alcohol.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 13:02:51', '2026-03-02 07:02:51'),
(43, '45ea663f6073ad7cb32b2bf0dfedfe8e05e5058d0c966615019fdd4d130b096c', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 5:3\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْمَيْتَةُ وَٱلدَّمُ وَلَحْمُ ٱلْخِنزِيرِ وَمَآ أُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ ٱللَّهِ بِهِۦ وَٱلْمُنْخَنِقَةُ وَٱلْمَوْقُوذَةُ وَٱلْمُتَرَدِّيَةُ وَٱلنَّطِيحَةُ وَمَآ أَكَلَ ٱلسَّبُعُ إِلَّا مَا ذَكَّيْتُمْ وَمَا ذُبِحَ عَلَى ٱلنُّصُبِ وَأَن تَسْتَقْسِمُوا۟ بِٱلْأَزْلَـٰمِ ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ فِسْقٌ ۗ ٱلْيَوْمَ يَئِسَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مِن دِينِكُمْ فَلَا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَٱخْشَوْنِ ۚ ٱلْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ وَأَتْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِى وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ ٱلْإِسْلَـٰمَ دِينًا ۚ فَمَنِ ٱضْطُرَّ فِى مَخْمَصَةٍ غَيْرَ مُتَجَانِفٍ لِّإِثْمٍ ۙ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"Prohibited to you are dead animals, blood, the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than Allah, and [those animals] killed by strangling or by a violent blow or by a head-long fall or by the goring of horns, and those from which a wild animal has eaten, except what you [are able to] slaughter [before its death], and those which are sacrificed on stone altars, and [prohibited is] that you seek decision through divining arrows. That is grave disobedience. This day those who disbelieve have despaired of [defeating] your religion; so fear them not, but fear Me. This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you and have approved for you Islam as religion. But whoever is forced by severe hunger with no inclination to sin - then indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 5:3\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Surah 5:3, eating pig meat is prohibited. The verse states: \\\"And the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than Allah...\\\" This indicates that consuming pig meat is considered haram (forbidden) in Islam.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 13:03:45', '2026-03-02 07:03:45'),
(44, 'a54c6040a875f7f59551b2941e9966381743e44318590dbfc63ffd20b6977853', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:178\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْقِصَاصُ فِى ٱلْقَتْلَى ۖ ٱلْحُرُّ بِٱلْحُرِّ وَٱلْعَبْدُ بِٱلْعَبْدِ وَٱلْأُنثَىٰ بِٱلْأُنثَىٰ ۚ فَمَنْ عُفِىَ لَهُۥ مِنْ أَخِيهِ شَىْءٌ فَٱتِّبَاعٌۢ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ وَأَدَآءٌ إِلَيْهِ بِإِحْسَـٰنٍ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ تَخْفِيفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ ۗ فَمَنِ ٱعْتَدَىٰ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ فَلَهُۥ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"O you who have believed, prescribed for you is legal retribution for those murdered - the free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female. But whoever overlooks from his brother anything, then there should be a suitable follow-up and payment to him with good conduct. This is an alleviation from your Lord and a mercy. But whoever transgresses after that will have a painful punishment.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 2:178\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[13],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Surah 2:178, the concept of \\\"follow-up\\\" (اتِّباعٌ) refers to a suitable action taken after a wrongdoing, such as murder. It involves making amends and showing good conduct to the victim\'s family. This is a mercy from Allah, allowing for forgiveness and alleviation of punishment. However, if the wrongdoer continues to transgress, they will face a painful punishment.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 20:35:40', '2026-03-02 14:35:40'),
(45, '73d35d20d01fc042a2037022218ea1e6e778fedf05d5629effa6cd57355368fb', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"informational_lookup\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah 4:15\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَٱلَّـٰتِى يَأْتِينَ ٱلْفَـٰحِشَةَ مِن نِّسَآئِكُمْ فَٱسْتَشْهِدُوا۟ عَلَيْهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةً مِّنكُمْ ۖ فَإِن شَهِدُوا۟ فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ فِى ٱلْبُيُوتِ حَتَّىٰ يَتَوَفَّىٰهُنَّ ٱلْمَوْتُ أَوْ يَجْعَلَ ٱللَّهُ لَهُنَّ سَبِيلًا\",\"english\":\"Those who commit unlawful sexual intercourse of your women - bring against them four [witnesses] from among you. And if they testify, confine the guilty women to houses until death takes them or Allah ordains for them [another] way.\",\"reference\":\"Surah 4:15\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\"}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[20],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"According to Surah 4:15, if a woman is accused of adultery, four witnesses from her community must testify against her. If they testify, she is confined to her home until death or Allah provides an alternative solution. This excerpt does not mention a reward for committing adultery. It focuses on the consequences and punishment for those accused of adultery.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false}', '2026-03-02 20:36:30', '2026-03-02 14:36:30');
