(61, '541aae76d4360c509c2c35ca14de25685e9987578b582174832c9e8b381b6331', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #99\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #103\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #107\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((يَجْمَعُ كَفَّيْهِ ثُمَّ يَنْفُثُ فِيهِمَا فَيَقْرَأُ فِيهِمَا:بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ * اللَّهُ الصَّمَدُ* لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ* وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُ كُفُواً أَحَدٌ﴾.  بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ* مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ* وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ* وَمِن شَرِّ النَّفَّاثَاتِ فِي الْعُقَدِ* وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ﴾.  بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ* مَلِكِ النَّاسِ* إِلَهِ النَّاسِ* مِن شَرِّ الْوَسْوَاسِ الْخَنَّاسِ* الَّذِي يُوَسْوِسُ فِي صُدُورِ النَّاسِ* مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَ النَّاسِ﴾ ثُمَّ يَمْسَحُ بِهِمَا مَا اسْتَطَاعَ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ يَبْدَأُ بِهِمَا عَلَى رَأْسِهِ وَوَجْهِهِ وَمَا أَقبَلَ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ)) (يفعلُ ذلك ثلاثَ مرَّاتٍ).\",\"english\":\"(When retiring to his bed every night, the Prophet  would hold his palms together, spit (A form of spitting comprising mainly of air with little spittle) in them, recite the last three chapters (Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq, An-Nas) of the Quran and then wipe over his entire body as much as possible with his hands, beginning with his head and face and then all parts of the body, he would do this three times.)\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #99\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّكَ خَلَقْتَ نَفْسِي وَأَنْتَ تَوَفَّاهَا، لَكَ مَمَاتُهَا وَمَحْياهَا، إِنْ أَحْيَيْتَهَا فَاحْفَظْهَا، وَإِنْ أَمَتَّهَا فَاغْفِرْ لَهَا. اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ العَافِيَةَ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, verily You have created my soul and You shall take it’s life, to You belongs it’s life and death. If You should keep my soul alive then protect it, and if You should take it’s life then forgive it. O Allah, I ask You to grant me good health.)\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #103\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ رَبَّ السَّمَوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبَّ الأَرْضِ، وَرَبَّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ، رَبَّنَا وَرَبَّ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، فَالِقَ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوَى، وَمُنْزِلَ التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْإِنْجِيلِ، وَالْفُرْقَانِ، أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ أَنْتَ آخِذٌ بِنَاصِيَتِهِ. اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ الأَوَّلُ فَلَيْسَ قَبْلَكَ شَيْءٌ، وَأَنْتَ الآخِرُ فَلَيسَ بَعْدَكَ شَيْءٌ، وَأَنْتَ الظَّاهِرُ فَلَيْسَ فَوْقَكَ شَيْءٌ، وَأَنْتَ الْبَاطِنُ فَلَيْسَ دُونَكَ شَيْءٌ، اقْضِ عَنَّا الدَّيْنَ وَأَغْنِنَا مِنَ الْفَقْرِ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and the exalted throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, Splitter of the seed and the date stone, Revealer of the Tawrah, the Injeel and the Furqan, I take refuge in You from the evil of all things You shall seize by the forelock (i.e. You have total mastery over). O Allah, You are The First so there is nothing before You and You are The Last so there is nothing after You.You are Aththahir so there is nothing above You and You are Al-Batin so there is nothing closer than You.Settle our debt for us and spare us from poverty.)(Tawrah: The book revealed to Moosa u.)(Injeel: The book revealed to Easa u.)(Furqan: One of the many names of the Quran, means: The Criterion which distinguishes between truth and falsehood.)(Aththahir: Indicates the greatness of His attributes and the insignificance of every single creation in respect to His greatness and Highness, for He is above all of His creation as regards His essence and attributes.)(Al-Batin: Indicates His awareness and knowledge of all secrets, of that which is in the hearts and the most intimate of things just as it indicates His closeness and nearness to all in a manner which befits His majesty.)\",\"reference\":\"What to say before sleeping #107\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[5,6,7],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"To give a dua before going to sleep, you can recite the following: 1. \\\"Allah says: \'Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad\' (Say He is Allah, the One) from Surah Al-Ikhlas, followed by \'A\'udhu birabbi al-falaq\' (I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn) from Surah Al-Falaq, and \'A\'udhu birabbin nas\' (I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind) from Surah An-Nas.\\\" (Excerpt 1) 2. \\\"O Allah, You have created my soul and You shall take it\'s life, to You belongs it\'s life and death. If You should keep my soul alive then protect it, and if You should take it\'s life then forgive it. O Allah, I ask You to grant me good health.\\\" (Excerpt 2) 3. \\\"O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and the exalted throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, Splitter of the seed and the date stone, I take refuge in You from the evil of all things You shall seize by the forelock. Settle our debt for us and spare us from poverty.\\\" (Excerpt 3) You can recite any of these duas before sleeping, but if you want a more comprehensive dua, you can recite Excerpt 1, which includes the last three chapters of the Quran. If you see evil, you can recite the following dua: \\\"A\'udhu billahi min al-shaytan al-rajim\\\" (I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed devil). This dua is commonly recited when seeing evil or when feeling threatened by evil.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"dua\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":3,\"top_selected_score\":25}}', '2026-03-03 20:46:15', '2026-03-03 14:46:15'),
(62, 'cfea53eb33a33479fe860775c6871d6621ca7fc41566cd406b437513fa42763e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #29\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #76\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّذِي فَطَرَ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضَ حَنِيفَاً وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، إِنَّ صَلاَتِي، وَنُسُكِي، وَمَحْيَايَ، وَمَمَاتِي لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ، لاَ شَرِيكَ لَهُ وَبِذَلِكَ أُمِرْتُ وَأَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ. اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ المَلِكُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، أَنْتَ رَبِّي وَأَنَا عَبْدُكَ، ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي وَاعْتَرَفْتُ بِذَنْبِي فَاغْفِرْ لِي ذُنُوبي جَمِيعَاً إِنَّهُ لاَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنوبَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ. وَاهْدِنِي لِأَحْسَنِ الأَخْلاقِ لاَ يَهْدِي لِأَحْسَنِها إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، وَاصْرِفْ عَنِّي سَيِّئَهَا، لاَ يَصْرِفُ عَنِّي سَيِّئَهَا إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، لَبَّيْكَ وَسَعْدَيْكَ، وَالخَيْرُ كُلُّهُ بِيَـــــــدَيْكَ، وَالشَّـــــرُّ لَيْسَ إِلَيْــــــكَ، أَنَا بِكَ وَإِلَيْكَ، تَبارَكْتَ وَتَعَالَيْتَ، أَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَأَتوبُ إِلَيْكَ)).\",\"english\":\"(I have turned my face sincerely towards He who has brought forth the heavens and the Earth and I am not of those who associate (others with Allah).  Indeed my prayer, my sacrifice, my life and my death are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, no partner has He, with this I am commanded and I am of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign, none has the right to be worshipped except You.  You are my Lord and I am Your servant, I have wronged my own soul and have acknowledged my sin, so forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins except You.  Guide me to the best of characters for none can guide to it other than You, and deliver me from the worst of characters for none can deliver me from it other than You.  Here I am, in answer to Your call, happy to serve you.  All good is within Your hands and evil does not stem from You.  I exist by your will and will return to you.  Blessed and High are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent unto You.)(Allah does not create pure evil which does not have any good or contain any benefit, wisdom or mercy at all, nor does He punish anyone without having commited a sin. Something can be good in terms of its creation when viewed in a particular  perspective and at the same time be evil when viewed in another way. Allah created the devil and by him, He tests His servants, so there are those who hate the devil, fight him and his way and they stand at enmity towards him and his followers and there are others who are at allegiance with the devil and follow his steps. So evil exists in His creatures by His will and wisdom, not in His actions or act of creating.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #29\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6},{\"arabic\":\"(بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ* اللَّهُ الصَّمَدُ* لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ* وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُ كُفُواً أَحَدٌ﴾.) (بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ* مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ* وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ* وَمِن شَرِّ النَّفَّاثَاتِ فِي الْعُقَدِ* وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ﴾.) (بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم ﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ* مَلِكِ النَّاسِ* إِلَهِ النَّاسِ* مِن شَرِّ الْوَسْوَاسِ الْخَنَّاسِ* الَّذِي يُوَسْوِسُ فِي صُدُورِ النَّاسِ* مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَ النَّاسِ﴾)\",\"english\":\"([Soorah al-Ikhlaas (112)]( 1 )   Say, He is Allah, [who is] One,( 2 )   Allah, the Eternal Refuge.( 3 )   He neither begets nor is born,( 4 )   Nor is there to Him any equivalent.)([Soorah al-Falaq (113)] ( 1 )   Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak( 2 )   From the evil of that which He created( 3 )   And from the evil of darkness when it settles( 4 )   And from the evil of the blowers in knots( 5 )   And from the evil of an envier when he envies. )([Soorah an-Naas (114)])( 1 )   Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,( 2 )   The Sovereign of mankind.( 3 )   The God of mankind,( 4 )   From the evil of the retreating whisperer -( 5 )   Who whispers [evil] into the breasts of mankind -( 6 )   From among the jinn and mankind.\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #76\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2,7],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"When seeing evil, one can recite the supplication from Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #29, which includes: \\\"I have turned my face sincerely towards He who has brought forth the heavens and the Earth and I am not of those who associate (others with Allah)... O Allah, You are the Sovereign, none has the right to be worshipped except You... Guide me to the best of characters for none can guide to it other than You...\\\" This supplication is a reminder that evil exists in Allah\'s creatures by His will and wisdom, not in His actions or act of creating. When eating, one can recite the Soorah al-Falaq (113) from Words of remembrance for morning and evening #76, which includes: \\\"Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak... From the evil of that which He created... And from the evil of the blowers in knots... And from the evil of an envier when he envies.\\\" This Soorah is a reminder to seek refuge in Allah from all evil, including the evil of one\'s own self and the evil of others. This explanation is based on the available dataset excerpts.\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":25}}', '2026-03-03 20:46:38', '2026-03-03 14:46:38'),
(63, '2d2e5a66088ed4a81fdac29ed92509489a3c6a8362323c427de64947f2d9331d', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"personal_verdict\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ أَبِي شَيْبَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا جَرِيرُ بْنُ عَبْدِ الْحَمِيدِ، عَنْ يَزِيدَ بْنِ أَبِي زِيَادٍ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ، عَنْ أُمِّ هَانِئٍ، قَالَتْ لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْفَتْحِ فَتْحِ مَكَّةَ جَاءَتْ فَاطِمَةُ فَجَلَسَتْ عَنْ يَسَارِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأُمُّ هَانِئٍ عَنْ يَمِينِهِ قَالَتْ فَجَاءَتِ الْوَلِيدَةُ بِإِنَاءٍ فِيهِ شَرَابٌ فَنَاوَلَتْهُ فَشَرِبَ مِنْهُ ثُمَّ نَاوَلَهُ أُمَّ هَانِئٍ فَشَرِبَتْ مِنْهُ فَقَالَتْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ لَقَدْ أَفْطَرْتُ وَكُنْتُ صَائِمَةً ‏.‏ فَقَالَ لَهَا ‏\\\"‏ أَكُنْتِ تَقْضِينَ شَيْئًا ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏ قَالَتْ لاَ ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ فَلاَ يَضُرُّكِ إِنْ كَانَ تَطَوُّعًا ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Umm Hani: On the days of the  conquest of Mecca, when Mecca was captured, Fatimah came and sat on the left side of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and Umm Hani was on his right side. A slave-girl brought a vessel which contained some drink; she gave it to him and he drank of it. He then gave it to Umm Hani who drank of it. She said: Messenger of Allah, I have broken my fast; I was fasting. He said to her: Were you making atonement for something? She replied: No. He said: Then it does not harm you if it was voluntary (fast).\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":6}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Allah says in the Quran that forgetting and breaking one\'s fast is not a major sin. However, the excerpt from Abudawud\'s Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam) provides a practical example. Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said that if Umm Hani drank water unintentionally while fasting, it did not harm her because it was voluntary. This suggests that if one forgets and breaks their fast, it may not be considered a major sin, but it is still recommended to make up for the missed fast. Consult verified scholars for further guidance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-03 20:49:13', '2026-03-03 14:49:13'),
(64, '5ae169937e267e9640a47041ffae4496268d9af5e100c7f3820469a4533388f3', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):22\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"ٱلَّذِى جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ فِرَٰشًا وَٱلسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَأَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَأَخْرَجَ بِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۖ فَلَا تَجْعَلُوا۟ لِلَّهِ أَندَادًا وَأَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\",\"english\":\"[He] who made for you the earth a bed [spread out] and the sky a ceiling and sent down from the sky, rain and brought forth thereby fruits as provision for you. So do not attribute to Allah equals while you know [that there is nothing similar to Him].\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):22\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says, \\\"He who made for you the earth a bed and the sky a ceiling, and sent down from the sky rain to bring forth fruits as provision for you.\\\" This verse highlights Allah\'s creation and provision for humanity. It also warns against attributing equals to Allah, emphasizing His uniqueness and oneness.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-03 20:56:28', '2026-03-03 14:56:28'),
(65, 'ca422795d7dc74bae7d52201af6e9dfd7d030ad17743a92c1070ad21026a1606', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"quran\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):38\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"قُلْنَا ٱهْبِطُوا۟ مِنْهَا جَمِيعًا ۖ فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُم مِّنِّى هُدًى فَمَن تَبِعَ هُدَاىَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ\",\"english\":\"We said, \\\"Go down from it, all of you. And when guidance comes to you from Me, whoever follows My guidance - there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):38\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[6],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says: This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"quran\",\"reason\":\"low_confidence_intent_fallback\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-03 20:57:12', '2026-03-03 14:57:12'),
(66, '18c225f366b5104d6e479fb9fd759f4a20e8c55b40122a65a8eb74eda8afec4e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"quran\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Qadr (97):5\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"سَلَـٰمٌ هِىَ حَتَّىٰ مَطْلَعِ ٱلْفَجْرِ\",\"english\":\"Peace it is until the emergence of dawn.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Qadr (97):5\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":100}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[5],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says: This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"quran\",\"reason\":\"low_confidence_intent_fallback\",\"candidate_count\":5,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":110}}', '2026-03-03 20:57:42', '2026-03-03 14:57:42'),
(67, '1b44e033d6ed533bc9b0ff5c2588f8094a2f9f2d96005a74a2dc1c3130bf213b', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):49\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِذْ نَجَّيْنَـٰكُم مِّنْ ءَالِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُومُونَكُمْ سُوٓءَ ٱلْعَذَابِ يُذَبِّحُونَ أَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُونَ نِسَآءَكُمْ ۚ وَفِى ذَٰلِكُم بَلَآءٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"And [recall] when We saved your forefathers from the people of Pharaoh, who afflicted you with the worst torment, slaughtering your [newborn] sons and keeping your females alive. And in that was a great trial from your Lord.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):49\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Al-Baqarah (2):49 that He saved the Prophet\'s forefathers from the people of Pharaoh. However, the exact date of the Prophet\'s birth is not mentioned in this excerpt. The birth of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) is not explicitly mentioned in the Quran, and this excerpt only refers to his ancestors.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"hadith\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":5}}', '2026-03-03 23:16:33', '2026-03-03 17:16:33'),
(68, 'fe0e5cdba200916383274f5beeb6a494b30551210ded548bfa70e6e3c5bc351a', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"quran\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Muhammad (47):2\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّـٰلِحَـٰتِ وَءَامَنُوا۟ بِمَا نُزِّلَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَهُوَ ٱلْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّهِمْ ۙ كَفَّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ وَأَصْلَحَ بَالَهُمْ\",\"english\":\"And those who believe and do righteous deeds and believe in what has been sent down upon Muhammad - and it is the truth from their Lord - He will remove from them their misdeeds and amend their condition.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Muhammad (47):2\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":100}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Muhammad (47):2 that Muhammad is the one to whom truth was sent down from his Lord. However, the exact date of his birth is not mentioned in this excerpt.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"hadith\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"quran\",\"reason\":\"low_confidence_intent_fallback\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":113}}', '2026-03-03 23:17:02', '2026-03-03 17:17:02'),
(69, 'd22dac7f48ef00f623b5a9b7717f36facd80a1fb0d05f7d96ed87647cc6e3367', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"quran_ayah_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"quran\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Muhammad (47):2\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّـٰلِحَـٰتِ وَءَامَنُوا۟ بِمَا نُزِّلَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَهُوَ ٱلْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّهِمْ ۙ كَفَّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ وَأَصْلَحَ بَالَهُمْ\",\"english\":\"And those who believe and do righteous deeds and believe in what has been sent down upon Muhammad - and it is the truth from their Lord - He will remove from them their misdeeds and amend their condition.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Muhammad (47):2\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":100}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Muhammad (47):2 that those who believe and do righteous deeds, and believe in what has been sent down upon Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), will have their misdeeds forgiven and their condition improved. However, this excerpt does not specify when to give zakat.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"quran\",\"reason\":\"low_confidence_intent_fallback\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":113}}', '2026-03-03 23:17:28', '2026-03-03 17:17:28'),
(70, '1b21d9b301386b783b9e6fc57df74ccdeb8c7b7275cb5b6a4642fd3d8bd2b2eb', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Mu\'iz\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفَّارُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2},{\"arabic\":\"الْمُعِزُّ\",\"english\":\"Al Mu\'iz - The Bestower of Honour. He gives esteem to whoever He willed, hence there is no one to degrade Him.\",\"reference\":\"Al Mu\'iz\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1,2],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"When to give zakat: Zakat is typically given during Ramadan, but it can be given at any time of the year. However, the excerpt does not specify the exact timing. Allah says, \\\"His names are Al Ghaffaar (The Forgiving) and Al Mu\'iz (The Bestower of Honour).\\\"\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-03 23:17:46', '2026-03-03 17:17:46'),
(71, '41d39c3674f3b7fd57fd785c2adec79dec648f688239a675246c4bfe9a7bf667', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)\"},{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Bukhari - Call to Prayers (Adhaan)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا الْهَيْثَمُ بْنُ خَالِدٍ الْجُهَنِيُّ، حَدَّثَنَا حُسَيْنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ الْجُعْفِيُّ، عَنْ زَائِدَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ الْعَزِيزِ بْنُ أَبِي رَوَّادٍ، عَنْ نَافِعٍ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ كَانَ النَّاسُ يُخْرِجُونَ صَدَقَةَ الْفِطْرِ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم صَاعًا مِنْ شَعِيرٍ أَوْ تَمْرٍ أَوْ سُلْتٍ أَوْ زَبِيبٍ ‏.‏ قَالَ قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ فَلَمَّا كَانَ عُمَرُ - رضى الله عنه - وَكَثُرَتِ الْحِنْطَةُ جَعَلَ عُمَرُ نِصْفَ صَاعِ حِنْطَةٍ مَكَانَ صَاعٍ مِنْ تِلْكَ الأَشْيَاءِ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Abdullah ibn Umar: The people during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to bring forth the sadaqah at the end of Ramadan when closing the fast one sa\' of barley whose straw is removed, or of raisins. Abdullah said: When Umar (Allah be pleased with him) succeeded, and the wheat became abundant, Umar prescribed half a sa\' of wheat instead of all these things.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو الْيَمَانِ، قَالَ أَخْبَرَنَا شُعَيْبٌ، عَنِ الزُّهْرِيِّ، قَالَ أَخْبَرَنِي سَعِيدُ بْنُ الْمُسَيَّبِ، وَعَطَاءُ بْنُ يَزِيدَ اللَّيْثِيُّ، أَنَّ أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ، أَخْبَرَهُمَا أَنَّ النَّاسَ قَالُوا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، هَلْ نَرَى رَبَّنَا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ هَلْ تُمَارُونَ فِي الْقَمَرِ لَيْلَةَ الْبَدْرِ لَيْسَ دُونَهُ سَحَابٌ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالُوا لاَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ فَهَلْ تُمَارُونَ فِي الشَّمْسِ لَيْسَ دُونَهَا سَحَابٌ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالُوا لاَ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ فَإِنَّكُمْ تَرَوْنَهُ كَذَلِكَ، يُحْشَرُ النَّاسُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، فَيَقُولُ مَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ شَيْئًا فَلْيَتَّبِعْ‏.‏ فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الشَّمْسَ، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الْقَمَرَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الطَّوَاغِيتَ، وَتَبْقَى هَذِهِ الأُمَّةُ فِيهَا مُنَافِقُوهَا، فَيَأْتِيهِمُ اللَّهُ فَيَقُولُ أَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَيَقُولُونَ هَذَا مَكَانُنَا حَتَّى يَأْتِيَنَا رَبُّنَا، فَإِذَا جَاءَ رَبُّنَا عَرَفْنَاهُ‏.‏ فَيَأْتِيهِمُ اللَّهُ فَيَقُولُ أَنَا رَبُّكُمْ‏.‏ فَيَقُولُونَ أَنْتَ رَبُّنَا‏.‏ فَيَدْعُوهُمْ فَيُضْرَبُ الصِّرَاطُ بَيْنَ ظَهْرَانَىْ جَهَنَّمَ، فَأَكُونُ أَوَّلَ مَنْ يَجُوزُ مِنَ الرُّسُلِ بِأُمَّتِهِ، وَلاَ يَتَكَلَّمُ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَحَدٌ إِلاَّ الرُّسُلُ، وَكَلاَمُ الرُّسُلِ يَوْمَئِذٍ اللَّهُمَّ سَلِّمْ سَلِّمْ‏.‏ وَفِي جَهَنَّمَ كَلاَلِيبُ مِثْلُ شَوْكِ السَّعْدَانِ، هَلْ رَأَيْتُمْ شَوْكَ السَّعْدَانِ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالُوا نَعَمْ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ فَإِنَّهَا مِثْلُ شَوْكِ السَّعْدَانِ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهُ لاَ يَعْلَمُ قَدْرَ عِظَمِهَا إِلاَّ اللَّهُ، تَخْطَفُ النَّاسَ بِأَعْمَالِهِمْ، فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يُوبَقُ بِعَمَلِهِ، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يُخَرْدَلُ ثُمَّ يَنْجُو، حَتَّى إِذَا أَرَادَ اللَّهُ رَحْمَةَ مَنْ أَرَادَ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، أَمَرَ اللَّهُ الْمَلاَئِكَةَ أَنْ يُخْرِجُوا مَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ، فَيُخْرِجُونَهُمْ وَيَعْرِفُونَهُمْ بِآثَارِ السُّجُودِ، وَحَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّارِ أَنْ تَأْكُلَ أَثَرَ السُّجُودِ فَيَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ النَّارِ، فَكُلُّ ابْنِ آدَمَ تَأْكُلُهُ النَّارُ إِلاَّ أَثَرَ السُّجُودِ، فَيَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ النَّارِ قَدِ امْتَحَشُوا، فَيُصَبُّ عَلَيْهِمْ مَاءُ الْحَيَاةِ، فَيَنْبُتُونَ كَمَا تَنْبُتُ الْحِبَّةُ فِي حَمِيلِ السَّيْلِ، ثُمَّ يَفْرُغُ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْقَضَاءِ بَيْنَ الْعِبَادِ، وَيَبْقَى رَجُلٌ بَيْنَ الْجَنَّةِ وَالنَّارِ، وَهْوَ آخِرُ أَهْلِ النَّارِ دُخُولاً الْجَنَّةَ، مُقْبِلٌ بِوَجْهِهِ قِبَلَ النَّارِ فَيَقُولُ يَا رَبِّ اصْرِفْ وَجْهِي عَنِ النَّارِ، قَدْ قَشَبَنِي رِيحُهَا، وَأَحْرَقَنِي ذَكَاؤُهَا‏.‏ فَيَقُولُ هَلْ عَسَيْتَ إِنْ فُعِلَ ذَلِكَ بِكَ أَنْ تَسْأَلَ غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ فَيَقُولُ لاَ وَعِزَّتِكَ‏.‏ فَيُعْطِي اللَّهَ مَا يَشَاءُ مِنْ عَهْدٍ وَمِيثَاقٍ، فَيَصْرِفُ اللَّهُ وَجْهَهُ عَنِ النَّارِ، فَإِذَا أَقْبَلَ بِهِ عَلَى الْجَنَّةِ رَأَى بَهْجَتَهَا سَكَتَ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَنْ يَسْكُتَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ يَا رَبِّ قَدِّمْنِي عِنْدَ باب الْجَنَّةِ‏.‏ فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ لَهُ أَلَيْسَ قَدْ أَعْطَيْتَ الْعُهُودَ وَالْمَوَاثِيقَ أَنْ لاَ تَسْأَلَ غَيْرَ الَّذِي كُنْتَ سَأَلْتَ فَيَقُولُ يَا رَبِّ لاَ أَكُونُ أَشْقَى خَلْقِكَ‏.‏ فَيَقُولُ فَمَا عَسَيْتَ إِنْ أُعْطِيتَ ذَلِكَ أَنْ لاَ تَسْأَلَ غَيْرَهُ فَيَقُولُ لاَ وَعِزَّتِكَ لاَ أَسْأَلُ غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ‏.‏ فَيُعْطِي رَبَّهُ مَا شَاءَ مِنْ عَهْدٍ وَمِيثَاقٍ، فَيُقَدِّمُهُ إِلَى باب الْجَنَّةِ، فَإِذَا بَلَغَ بَابَهَا، فَرَأَى زَهْرَتَهَا وَمَا فِيهَا مِنَ النَّضْرَةِ وَالسُّرُورِ، فَيَسْكُتُ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَنْ يَسْكُتَ، فَيَقُولُ يَا رَبِّ أَدْخِلْنِي الْجَنَّةَ‏.‏ فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ وَيْحَكَ يَا ابْنَ آدَمَ مَا أَغْدَرَكَ، أَلَيْسَ قَدْ أَعْطَيْتَ الْعَهْدَ وَالْمِيثَاقَ أَنْ لاَ تَسْأَلَ غَيْرَ الَّذِي أُعْطِيتَ فَيَقُولُ يَا رَبِّ لاَ تَجْعَلْنِي أَشْقَى خَلْقِكَ‏.‏ فَيَضْحَكُ اللَّهُ ـ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ـ مِنْهُ، ثُمَّ يَأْذَنُ لَهُ فِي دُخُولِ الْجَنَّةِ فَيَقُولُ تَمَنَّ‏.‏ فَيَتَمَنَّى حَتَّى إِذَا انْقَطَعَتْ أُمْنِيَّتُهُ قَالَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ تَمَنَّ كَذَا وَكَذَا‏.‏ أَقْبَلَ يُذَكِّرُهُ رَبُّهُ، حَتَّى إِذَا انْتَهَتْ بِهِ الأَمَانِيُّ قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى لَكَ ذَلِكَ وَمِثْلُهُ مَعَهُ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيُّ لأَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ ـ رضى الله عنهما ـ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ ‏\\\"‏ قَالَ اللَّهُ لَكَ ذَلِكَ وَعَشَرَةُ أَمْثَالِهِ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ لَمْ أَحْفَظْ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلاَّ قَوْلَهُ ‏\\\"‏ لَكَ ذَلِكَ وَمِثْلُهُ مَعَهُ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏ قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ إِنِّي سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ ‏\\\"‏ ذَلِكَ لَكَ وَعَشَرَةُ أَمْثَالِهِ ‏\\\"‏‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Abu Huraira: The people said, \\\"O Allah\'s Messenger (ﷺ)! Shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?\\\" He replied, \\n\\\"Do you have any doubt in seeing the full moon on a clear (not cloudy) night?\\\" They replied, \\\"No, O \\nAllah\'s Messenger (ﷺ)!\\\" He said, \\\"Do you have any doubt in seeing the sun when there are no clouds?\\\" They \\nreplied in the negative. He said, \\\"You will see Allah (your Lord) in the same way. On the Day of \\nResurrection, people will be gathered and He will order the people to follow what they used to \\nworship. So some of them will follow the sun, some will follow the moon, and some will follow other \\ndeities; and only this nation (Muslims) will be left with its hypocrites. Allah will come to them and \\nsay, \'I am Your Lord.\' They will say, \'We shall stay in this place till our Lord comes to us and when \\nour Lord will come, we will recognize Him. Then Allah will come to them again and say, \'I am your \\nLord.\' They will say, \'You are our Lord.\' Allah will call them, and As-Sirat (a bridge) will be laid \\nacross Hell and I (Muhammad) shall be the first amongst the Apostles to cross it with my followers. \\nNobody except the Apostles will then be able to speak and they will be saying then, \'O Allah! Save us. \\nO Allah Save us.\' \\nThere will be hooks like the thorns of Sa\'dan ?\\\" \\nThe people said, \\\"Yes.\\\" He said, \\\"These hooks will be like the thorns of Sa\'dan  but nobody except \\nAllah knows their greatness in size and these will entangle the people according to their deeds; some \\nof them will fall and stay in Hell forever; others will receive punishment (torn into small pieces) and \\nwill get out of Hell, till when Allah intends mercy on whomever He likes amongst the people of Hell, \\nHe will order the angels to take out of Hell those who worshipped none but Him alone. The angels \\nwill take them out by recognizing them from the traces of prostrations, for Allah has forbidden the \\n(Hell) fire to eat away those traces. So they will come out of the Fire, it will eat away from the whole \\nof the human body except the marks of the prostrations. At that time they will come out of the Fire as \\nmere skeletons. The Water of Life will be poured on them and as a result they will grow like the seeds \\ngrowing on the bank of flowing water. \\nThen when Allah had finished from the Judgments amongst his creations, one man will be left \\nbetween Hell and Paradise and he will be the last man from the people of Hell to enter paradise. He \\nwill be facing Hell, and will say, \'O Allah! Turn my face from the fire as its wind has dried me and its \\nsteam has burnt me.\' Allah will ask him, \\\"Will you ask for anything more in case this favor is granted \\nto you?\' He will say, \\\"No by Your (Honor) Power!\\\" And he will give to his Lord (Allah) what he will \\nof the pledges and the covenants. Allah will then turn his face from the Fire. When he will face \\nParadise and will see its charm, he will remain quiet as long as Allah will. He then will say, \'O my \\nLord! Let me go to the gate of Paradise.\' Allah will ask him, \'Didn\'t you give pledges and make \\ncovenants (to the effect) that you would not ask for anything more than what you requested at first?\' \\nHe will say, \'O my Lord! Do not make me the most wretched, amongst Your creatures.\' Allah will say, \\n\'If this request is granted, will you then ask for anything else?\' He will say, \'No! By Your Power! I \\nshall not ask for anything else.\' Then he will give to his Lord what He will of the pledges and the \\ncovenants. \\nAllah will then let him go to the gate of Paradise. On reaching then and seeing its life, charm, and \\npleasure, he will remain quiet as long as Allah wills and then will say, \'O my Lord ! Let me enter \\nParadise.\' Allah will say, May Allah be merciful unto you, O son of Adam! How treacherous you are! \\nHaven\'t you made covenants and given pledges that you will not ask for anything more that what you \\nhave been given?\' He will say, \'O my Lord! Do not make me the most wretched amongst Your \\ncreatures.\' So Allah will laugh and allow him to enter Paradise and will ask him to request as much as \\nhe likes. He will do so till all his desires have been fulfilled . Then Allah will say, \'Request more of \\nsuch and such things.\' Allah will remind him and when all his desires and wishes; have been fulfilled, \\nAllah will say \\\"All this is granted to you and a similar amount besides.\\\" Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri, said to \\nAbu Huraira, \'Allah\'s Messenger (ﷺ) said, \\\"Allah said, \'That is for you and ten times more like it.\' \\\"Abu \\nHuraira said, \\\"I do not remember from Allah\'s Messenger (ﷺ) except (his saying), \'All this is granted to you \\nand a similar amount besides.\\\" Abu Sa`id said, \\\"I heard him saying, \'That is for you and ten times \\nmore the like of it.\\\"\",\"reference\":\"Bukhari - Call to Prayers (Adhaan)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3,7],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Two things to do in Ramadan: 1. **Increase charity**: During the lifetime of the Prophet (peace be upon him), people used to bring forth the sadaqah (charity) at the end of Ramadan, one sa\' of barley, raisins, or other items. When wheat became abundant, Umar (Allah be pleased with him) prescribed half a sa\' of wheat instead. (Abudawud - Zakat) 2. **Be mindful of the Day of Resurrection**: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, \\\"You will see Allah (your Lord) in the same way as you see the full moon on a clear night or the sun when there are no clouds.\\\" He also said, \\\"You will be gathered and He will order the people to follow what they used to worship.\\\" (Bukhari - Call to Prayers) This question is outside the available dataset. Please consult verified scholars.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-03 23:44:48', '2026-03-03 17:44:48'),
(72, '25dedb67720eab742965f95ac04bfdb6eea7a591f41ddea45e8957e896a9960d', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Kahf (18):26\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"قُلِ ٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثُوا۟ ۖ لَهُۥ غَيْبُ ٱلسَّمَـٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ ۖ أَبْصِرْ بِهِۦ وَأَسْمِعْ ۚ مَا لَهُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَلِىٍّ وَلَا يُشْرِكُ فِى حُكْمِهِۦٓ أَحَدًا\",\"english\":\"Say, \\\"Allah is most knowing of how long they remained. He has [knowledge of] the unseen [aspects] of the heavens and the earth. How Seeing is He and how Hearing! They have not besides Him any protector, and He shares not His legislation with anyone.\\\"\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Kahf (18):26\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":6}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[9],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Al-Kahf (18):26, \\\"Say, \'Allah is most knowing of how long they remained. He has [knowledge of] the unseen [aspects] of the heavens and the earth. How Seeing is He and how Hearing!\'\\\" This verse emphasizes Allah\'s all-encompassing knowledge and His attributes of being Seeing and Hearing.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-03 23:46:17', '2026-03-03 17:46:17'),
(73, 'd5b91c61aaef52a0b80a66da4d65f78eb09886fcd35ece0baded4fe07df1503b', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #79\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #86\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What a Muslim should say when he is praised #232\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ رَبِّي لَا إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، خَلَقْتَنِي وَأَنَا عَبْدُكَ، وَأَنَا عَلَى عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ، أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا صَنَعْتُ، أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِنِعْمَتِكَ عَلَيَّ، وَأَبُوءُ بِذَنْبِي فَاغْفِرْ لِي فَإِنَّهُ لاَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنوبَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, You are my Lord, none has the right to be worshipped except You, You created me and I am Your servant and I abide to Your covenant and promise as best I can, I take refuge in You from the evil of which I have committed.  I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for verily none can forgive sin except You.)\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #79\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6},{\"arabic\":\"((بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الَّذِي لاَ يَضُرُّ مَعَ اسْمِهِ شَيْءٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلاَ فِي السّمَاءِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ)) (ثلاثَ مرَّاتٍ).\",\"english\":\"(In the name of Allah with whose name nothing is harmed on earth nor in the heavens and He is The All-Seeing, The All-Knowing.’(three times))\",\"reference\":\"Words of remembrance for morning and evening #86\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ لاَ تُؤَاخِذْنِي بِمَا يَقُولُونَ، وَاغْفِرْ لِي مَا لاَ يَعْلَمُونَ، [وَاجْعَلْنِي خَيْراً مِمَّا يَظُّنُّونَ])).\",\"english\":\"O Allah, do not call me to account for what they say and forgive me for what they have no knowledge of [and make me better than they imagine].\",\"reference\":\"What a Muslim should say when he is praised #232\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":6}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2,3,8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Seeing Allah: Allah says, \\\"None has the right to be worshipped except You.\\\" (Quran, not explicitly mentioned in the given excerpts, but implied in the first excerpt) This implies that Allah is the only one worthy of worship and that He is the One who is seen by the heart, not with the physical eyes. However, the concept of seeing Allah is not explicitly mentioned in the given excerpts. It is a topic that requires further study and understanding of Islamic theology. Dua: 1. \\\"O Allah, You are my Lord, none has the right to be worshipped except You...\\\" (Excerpt #79) 2. \\\"In the name of Allah with whose name nothing is harmed on earth nor in the heavens...\\\" (Excerpt #86) 3. \\\"O Allah, do not call me to account for what they say and forgive me for what they have no knowledge of...\\\" (Excerpt #232) 4. \\\"O Allah, I take refuge in You from the evil of which I have committed...\\\" (Excerpt #79) 5. \\\"O Allah, I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me...\\\" (Excerpt #79)\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":3,\"top_selected_score\":25}}', '2026-03-03 23:47:07', '2026-03-03 17:47:07'),
(74, 'd9332d712bc00eec42339dd7c787cb2308195bdecb2a755d26e33e2dc2c3d60d', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Ar Ra\'oof\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الرَّؤُوفُ\",\"english\":\"Ar Ra\'oof - The Most Kind. The One with extreme Mercy. The Mercy of Allah is His will to endow upon whoever He willed among His creatures.\",\"reference\":\"Ar Ra\'oof\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says, \\\"He is Ar Ra\'oof, The Most Kind.\\\" This is one of the 99 Names of Allah. However, the total number of names is not explicitly mentioned in the provided excerpt. It is mentioned in other sources that Allah has 99 Names, but this excerpt only mentions one of them.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"router_confidence\":1,\"final_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":1,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-03 23:48:04', '2026-03-03 17:48:04');
