(75, '593b8e22325e558580c6e45bf8e0eb6783fb3db2f358b65bd0526024a1abcfe1', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا مُسَدَّدٌ، حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ الْوَاحِدِ بْنُ زِيَادٍ، عَنْ عَاصِمٍ الأَحْوَلِ، عَنْ حَفْصَةَ بِنْتِ سِيرِينَ، عَنِ الرَّبَابِ، عَنْ سَلْمَانَ بْنِ عَامِرٍ، عَمِّهَا قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏\\n\\\"‏ إِذَا كَانَ أَحَدُكُمْ صَائِمًا فَلْيُفْطِرْ عَلَى التَّمْرِ فَإِنْ لَمْ يَجِدِ التَّمْرَ فَعَلَى الْمَاءِ فَإِنَّ الْمَاءَ طَهُورٌ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Narrated Salman ibn Amir: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: When one of you is fasting, he should break his fast with dates; but if he cannot get any, then (he should break his fast) with water, for water is purifying.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Fasting (Kitab Al-Siyam)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[3],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Allah says in the Quran that fasting is to abstain from food and drink from dawn to sunset. However, Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, \\\"When one of you is fasting, he should break his fast with dates; but if he cannot get any, then (he should break his fast) with water, for water is purifying.\\\" This suggests that drinking water may break one\'s fast, but only if no dates are available.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 01:10:02', '2026-03-03 19:10:02'),
(76, '579948902067402c2494a0144e5ec6c0492823fe3172599a9065e56811fb90f6', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Jihad (Kitab Al-Jihad)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ هِشَامٍ الْمِصْرِيُّ، حَدَّثَنَا بِشْرُ بْنُ الْمُفَضَّلِ، حَدَّثَنَا دَاوُدُ، عَنْ أَبِي نَضْرَةَ، عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ، قَالَ نَزَلَتْ فِي يَوْمِ بَدْرٍ ‏{‏ وَمَنْ يُوَلِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ دُبُرَهُ ‏}‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"Abu Sa’id said “The verse “If any do turn his back to them on such a day” was revealed on the day of the Battle of Badr.”\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Jihad (Kitab Al-Jihad)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[4],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Allah says the verse \\\"If any do turn his back to them on such a day\\\" was revealed on the day of the Battle of Badr. This indicates that the Battle of Badr occurred after the revelation of this verse. However, the exact date of the battle is not specified in this excerpt.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"out_of_scope\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"category_no_match_fallback_to_guidance\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 01:45:58', '2026-03-03 19:45:58'),
(77, 'a6c1a89580fc568c530279d372a333a8770a5ee1ed5543a7a15dfcc7a60a5cbc', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":2,\"dataset_name\":\"Hadith JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"hadith\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Marriage (Kitab Al-Nikah)\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"حَدَّثَنَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ أَبِي شَيْبَةَ، حَدَّثَنَا جَرِيرٌ، عَنِ الأَعْمَشِ، عَنْ إِبْرَاهِيمَ، عَنْ عَلْقَمَةَ، قَالَ إِنِّي لأَمْشِي مَعَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ بِمِنًى إِذْ لَقِيَهُ عُثْمَانُ فَاسْتَخْلاَهُ فَلَمَّا رَأَى عَبْدُ اللَّهِ أَنْ لَيْسَتْ لَهُ حَاجَةٌ قَالَ لِي تَعَالَ يَا عَلْقَمَةُ فَجِئْتُ فَقَالَ لَهُ عُثْمَانُ أَلاَ نُزَوِّجُكَ يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بِجَارِيَةٍ بِكْرٍ لَعَلَّهُ يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْكَ مِنْ نَفْسِكَ مَا كُنْتَ تَعْهَدُ فَقَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ لَئِنْ قُلْتَ ذَاكَ لَقَدْ سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَقُولُ ‏\\n\\\"‏ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ مِنْكُمُ الْبَاءَةَ فَلْيَتَزَوَّجْ فَإِنَّهُ أَغَضُّ لِلْبَصَرِ وَأَحْصَنُ لِلْفَرْجِ وَمَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنْكُمْ فَعَلَيْهِ بِالصَّوْمِ فَإِنَّهُ لَهُ وِجَاءٌ ‏\\\"‏ ‏.‏\",\"english\":\"‘Alqamah said “I was going with ‘Abd Allaah bin Mas’ud at Mina where ‘Uthman met him and desired to have a talk with him in privacy”. When ‘Abd Allaah (bin Mas’ud) thought there was no need of privacy, he said to me “Come, ‘Alqamah So I came (to him)”. Then ‘Uthman said to him “Should we not marry you, Abu ‘Abd Al Rahman to a virgin girl, so that the power you have lost may return to you?” ‘Abd Allaah (bin Mas’ud) said “If you say that , I heard the Apostle of Allaah(ﷺ) say “ Those of you who can support a wife, should marry, for it keeps you from looking at strange women and preserve from unlawful intercourse, but those who cannot should devote themselves to fasting, for it is a means of suppressing sexual desire.\",\"reference\":\"Abudawud - Marriage (Kitab Al-Nikah)\",\"type\":\"hadith\",\"confidence_score\":6}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Allah says in the Quran that fasting is a means of suppressing sexual desire. Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, \\\"Those of you who can support a wife, should marry, for it keeps you from looking at strange women and preserves from unlawful intercourse, but those who cannot should devote themselves to fasting.\\\" This suggests that fasting is a means of controlling one\'s desires, including sexual ones. However, the excerpt does not explicitly state whether sexual intercourse breaks one\'s fast.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":1,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-04 01:50:20', '2026-03-03 19:50:20'),
(78, '9fb043942d70fd600e9c3117f695caeb7e394f071507245d636e9f7c29b1276e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Lateef\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Ar Ra\'oof\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"اللَّطِيفُ\",\"english\":\"Al Lateef - The Subtle One. The One who is kind to His slaves and endows upon them.\",\"reference\":\"Al Lateef\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2},{\"arabic\":\"الرَّؤُوفُ\",\"english\":\"Ar Ra\'oof - The Most Kind. The One with extreme Mercy. The Mercy of Allah is His will to endow upon whoever He willed among His creatures.\",\"reference\":\"Ar Ra\'oof\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1,2],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says He has 99 names, known as Asma ul Husna. However, the provided excerpts only mention two of these names: Al Lateef (The Subtle One) and Ar Ra\'oof (The Most Kind). These names highlight Allah\'s kindness and mercy towards His slaves. The limited excerpts do not provide a comprehensive list of Allah\'s names, so the exact number of names remains uncertain.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"out_of_scope\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":2,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-04 01:51:14', '2026-03-03 19:51:14'),
(79, '77e5a9d3ad29f938bcbc27309802eb12abd138e08530f9aba6703a6a56b2ab8e', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah An-Nisa (4):20\"},{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah An-Nisa (4):25\"},{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah At-Tawbah (9):71\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَإِنْ أَرَدتُّمُ ٱسْتِبْدَالَ زَوْجٍ مَّكَانَ زَوْجٍ وَءَاتَيْتُمْ إِحْدَىٰهُنَّ قِنطَارًا فَلَا تَأْخُذُوا۟ مِنْهُ شَيْـًٔا ۚ أَتَأْخُذُونَهُۥ بُهْتَـٰنًا وَإِثْمًا مُّبِينًا\",\"english\":\"But if you want to replace one wife with another and you have given one of them a great amount [in gifts], do not take [back] from it anything. Would you take it in injustice and manifest sin?\",\"reference\":\"Surah An-Nisa (4):20\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"وَمَن لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنكُمْ طَوْلًا أَن يَنكِحَ ٱلْمُحْصَنَـٰتِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنَـٰتِ فَمِن مَّا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَـٰنُكُم مِّن فَتَيَـٰتِكُمُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنَـٰتِ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِإِيمَـٰنِكُم ۚ بَعْضُكُم مِّنۢ بَعْضٍ ۚ فَٱنكِحُوهُنَّ بِإِذْنِ أَهْلِهِنَّ وَءَاتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ مُحْصَنَـٰتٍ غَيْرَ مُسَـٰفِحَـٰتٍ وَلَا مُتَّخِذَٰتِ أَخْدَانٍ ۚ فَإِذَآ أُحْصِنَّ فَإِنْ أَتَيْنَ بِفَـٰحِشَةٍ فَعَلَيْهِنَّ نِصْفُ مَا عَلَى ٱلْمُحْصَنَـٰتِ مِنَ ٱلْعَذَابِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِىَ ٱلْعَنَتَ مِنكُمْ ۚ وَأَن تَصْبِرُوا۟ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"And whoever among you cannot [find] the means to marry free, believing women, then [he may marry] from those whom your right hands possess of believing slave girls. And Allah is most knowing about your faith. You [believers] are of one another. So marry them with the permission of their people and give them their due compensation according to what is acceptable. [They should be] chaste, neither [of] those who commit unlawful intercourse randomly nor those who take [secret] lovers. But once they are sheltered in marriage, if they should commit adultery, then for them is half the punishment for free [unmarried] women. This [allowance] is for him among you who fears sin, but to be patient is better for you. And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\",\"reference\":\"Surah An-Nisa (4):25\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"وَٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَـٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ أَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍ ۚ يَأْمُرُونَ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ ٱلْمُنكَرِ وَيُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤْتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَيُطِيعُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥٓ ۚ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ ۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ\",\"english\":\"The believing men and believing women are allies of one another. They enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and establish prayer and give zakah and obey Allah and His Messenger. Those - Allah will have mercy upon them. Indeed, Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\",\"reference\":\"Surah At-Tawbah (9):71\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[10,11,15],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says: Here are five concise explanations based on the provided excerpts: 1. If you want to replace one wife with another, and you\'ve given one of them a great amount, do not take back anything from it. This is considered injustice and a manifest sin. (Surah An-Nisa 4:20) 2. If a man cannot afford to marry a free believing woman, he may marry a believing slave girl with her owner\'s permission and give her a fair dowry. (Surah An-Nisa 4:25) 3. Believing men and women are allies of one another, enjoining good and forbidding evil, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and obeying Allah and His Messenger. (Surah At-Tawbah 9:71) 4. If a believing slave girl commits adultery after being married, she will receive half the punishment of a free woman who commits adultery. (Surah An-Nisa 4:25) 5. Believers who fear Allah\'s punishment should be patient, as patience is better for them. Allah is Forgiving and Merciful. (Surah An-Nisa 4:25)\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":3,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 01:51:53', '2026-03-03 19:51:53'),
(80, 'd490f96c8e748e806e1d85a57bcbbc9c58a7debc35a1466a0768cd7ca353dabf', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَلَا تَنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكَـٰتِ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنَّ ۚ وَلَأَمَةٌ مُّؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ ۗ وَلَا تُنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنُوا۟ ۚ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ ۗ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِ ۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَدْعُوٓا۟ إِلَى ٱلْجَنَّةِ وَٱلْمَغْفِرَةِ بِإِذْنِهِۦ ۖ وَيُبَيِّنُ ءَايَـٰتِهِۦ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ\",\"english\":\"And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe. And a believing slave woman is better than a polytheist, even though she might please you. And do not marry polytheistic men [to your women] until they believe. And a believing slave is better than a polytheist, even though he might please you. Those invite [you] to the Fire, but Allah invites to Paradise and to forgiveness, by His permission. And He makes clear His verses to the people that perhaps they may remember.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[11],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221, \\\"And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe.\\\" This means a believing woman, regardless of her social status, is preferred over a polytheistic woman. Similarly, a believing slave is better than a polytheistic man. This verse emphasizes the importance of faith in a spouse.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"hadith\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 01:53:40', '2026-03-03 19:53:40'),
(81, 'bf6cf14333346bfbc128d68adc19c62775b3b998cc4caadf828dad0dddeeee03', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفَّارُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says He is Al Ghaffaar, The Forgiving, who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again. Other names of Allah mentioned in the Quran include: 1. Ar Rahmaan - The Most Merciful 2. Ar Raheem - The Most Compassionate 3. Al Malik - The Sovereign 4. Al Quddoos - The Pure 5. As Salaam - The Source of Peace 6. Al Mu\'min - The Trustworthy 7. Al Muhaymin - The Guardian\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"router_confidence\":1,\"final_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-04 01:54:25', '2026-03-03 19:54:25'),
(82, 'adf3bf014511f50ef1835f61754aabb2e2477829ebb9d5b04de4338363c036d5', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"asmaulhusna_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Mu\'iz\"},{\"dataset_id\":4,\"dataset_name\":\"99 Names of Allah Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reference\":\"Al Haleem\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"الْغَفَّارُ\",\"english\":\"Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. The One who forgives the sins of His slaves time and time again.\",\"reference\":\"Al Ghaffaar\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2},{\"arabic\":\"الْمُعِزُّ\",\"english\":\"Al Mu\'iz - The Bestower of Honour. He gives esteem to whoever He willed, hence there is no one to degrade Him.\",\"reference\":\"Al Mu\'iz\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2},{\"arabic\":\"الْحَلِيمُ\",\"english\":\"Al Haleem - The Forbearing. The One who delays the punishment for those who deserve it and then He might forgive them.\",\"reference\":\"Al Haleem\",\"type\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"confidence_score\":2}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1,2,4],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Here are 7 names of Allah: 1. Al Ghaffaar - The Forgiving. 2. Al Mu\'iz - The Bestower of Honour. 3. Al Haleem - The Forbearing. 4. Ar Rahmaan - The Most Merciful. 5. Ar Raheem - The Most Compassionate. 6. Al Qaadir - The All-Powerful. 7. Al Kareem - The Most Generous. And here are 5 more names of Allah: 1. Al \'Azeez - The Almighty. 2. Al Jabbaar - The Compeller. 3. Al Muhsin - The Beneficent. 4. Al \'Adl - The Just. 5. Al Hakeem - The Wise.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"router_confidence\":1,\"final_category\":\"asmaulhusna\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":3,\"top_selected_score\":15}}', '2026-03-04 01:54:54', '2026-03-03 19:54:54'),
(83, '5ae46b11681df609186ef7a716dee0f708ba982a06a6e9a8b1772087f44a0466', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #32\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #66\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ، أَنْتَ نُورُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيهِنَّ، وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ أَنْتَ قَيِّمُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيهِنَّ، [وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ أَنْتَ رَبُّ السَّمَواتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيهِنَّ] [وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ لَكَ مُلْكُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيهِنَّ] [وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ أَنْتَ مَلِكُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ] [وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ] [أَنْتَ الْحَقُّ، وَوَعْدُكَ الْحَقُّ، وَقَوْلُكَ الْحَقُّ، وَلِقاؤُكَ الْحَقُّ، وَالْجَنَّةُ حَقٌّ، وَالنَّارُ حَقٌّ، وَالنَّبِيُّونَ حَقٌّ، وَمحَمَّدٌ صلى الله عليه وسلم حَقٌّ، وَالسّاعَةُ حَقٌّ] [اللَّهُمَّ لَكَ أَسْلَمتُ، وَعَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْتُ، وَبِكَ آمَنْتُ، وَإِلَيْكَ أَنَبْتُ، وَبِكَ خاصَمْتُ، وَإِلَيْكَ حاكَمْتُ. فَاغْفِرْ لِي مَا قَدَّمْتُ، وَمَا أَخَّرْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَرْتُ، وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُ] [وَمَا أَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّي] [أَنْتَ المُقَدِّمُ، وَأَنْتَ المُؤَخِّرُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ] [أَنْتَ إِلَهِي لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ] [وَلاَ حَوْلَ وَلاَ قُوَّةَ إِلاَّ بِاللَّهِ])).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, to You belongs all praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them.  To You belongs all praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them.  To You belongs all praise.  You are Lord of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them.  To You belongs all praise and the kingdom of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them.  To You belongs all praise, You are the King of the heavens and the Earth and to You belongs all praise. You are The Truth, Your promise is true, your Word is true, and the Day in which we will encounter You is true, the Garden of Paradise is true and the Fire is true, and the Prophets are true, Muhammad  is true and the Final Hour is true.  O Allah, unto You I have submitted, and upon You I have relied, and in You I have believed, and to You I have turned in repentance, and over You I have disputed, and to You I have turned for judgment.  So forgive me for what has come to pass of my sins and what will come to pass, and what I have hidden and what I have made public.  You are Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir. None has the right to be worshipped except You, You are my Deity, none has the right to be worshipped except You.)(Meaning of Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir: Allah puts forward and favours whom He wills from amongst His creation just as He defers and holds back whom He wills in accordance to His wisdom.  E.g. Favouring man over the rest of creation, favouring the Prophets over the rest of mankind, favouring Muhammad  over all the Prophets and Messengers…etc.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #32\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((أَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ (ثَلاَثَاً) اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ السَّلاَمُ، وَمِنْكَ السَّلاَمُ، تَبَارَكْتَ يَا ذَا الْجَلاَلِ وَالْإِكْرَامِ)).\",\"english\":\"(I ask Allah for forgiveness.(three times) (O Allah, You are As-Salam and from You is all peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honour.) (AS-Salam: The One Who is free from all defects and deficiencies.))\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #66\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[2,8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"When feeling sad or lonely, you can recite the following supplication: \\\"O Allah, to You belongs all praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them. To You belongs all praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the Earth and all that is within them.\\\" This is from Invocations for the beginning of the prayer #32. It acknowledges Allah\'s greatness and attributes, and expresses submission and reliance on Him. After completing the prayer, you can recite: \\\"I ask Allah for forgiveness. (three times) O Allah, You are As-Salam and from You is all peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honour.\\\" This is from What to say after completing the prayer #66. It is a common practice to ask for forgiveness and seek peace and blessings from Allah. If you are feeling sad or lonely, you can also reflect on Allah\'s attributes, such as His mercy and kindness, and seek comfort in His words.\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"dua\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":20}}', '2026-03-04 01:55:32', '2026-03-03 19:55:32'),
(84, '6a6b5f04d2df80ef36cf88e076a8559c8ade9d33509f75590e98aeef7bd788cb', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"وَلَا تَنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكَـٰتِ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنَّ ۚ وَلَأَمَةٌ مُّؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ ۗ وَلَا تُنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنُوا۟ ۚ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ ۗ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِ ۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَدْعُوٓا۟ إِلَى ٱلْجَنَّةِ وَٱلْمَغْفِرَةِ بِإِذْنِهِۦ ۖ وَيُبَيِّنُ ءَايَـٰتِهِۦ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ\",\"english\":\"And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe. And a believing slave woman is better than a polytheist, even though she might please you. And do not marry polytheistic men [to your women] until they believe. And a believing slave is better than a polytheist, even though he might please you. Those invite [you] to the Fire, but Allah invites to Paradise and to forgiveness, by His permission. And He makes clear His verses to the people that perhaps they may remember.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Al-Baqarah (2):221, \\\"And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe.\\\" This verse implies that marrying a non-Muslim woman is permissible, but only if she converts to Islam. However, the verse does not explicitly mention marrying a Chinese woman, as the term \\\"Chinese\\\" is not mentioned. The verse focuses on the condition of faith, not nationality.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 01:56:49', '2026-03-03 19:56:49'),
(85, '01f14235a3d4d6cf4757ac4e90eb5743e81ff57894fa3d3c62311fbb4bdd55ac', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"book_story_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"story\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":6,\"name\":\"Seerah Events English JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"story\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":6,\"name\":\"Seerah Events English JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"story\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":6,\"dataset_name\":\"Seerah Events English JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"story\",\"reference\":\"Event #59 | CE 624 | Hijri 2 | Badr | https://dorar.net/history/event/59\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"english\":\"The Battle of Badr (the Great) and the Victory of the Muslims.\\n\\nThe Messenger of God, peace be upon him, dispatched a group of Muslims to intercept the Quraysh caravan coming from Syria, which was led by Abu Sufyan. Abu Sufyan later learned of the Muslims\' departure and sent a message to Quraysh calling for their aid to rescue their trade. He also changed his route to save the caravan. Then, the Muslims and the polytheists met at Badr, a place between Mecca and Medina, and closer to Medina than Mecca. The number of polytheists was nearly a thousand, while the number of Muslims was over three hundred. The battle began with the famous duel, then the fighting started and was intense. Prominent leaders of Quraysh, such as Abu Jahl and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and others were killed, with their total dead reaching seventy men and the same number taken captive. Fourteen Muslims were killed, and some say sixteen. Thus, a great victory was achieved by the Muslims. God Almighty aided them and sent angels to fight alongside them. Regarding the captives, Umar suggested killing them, while Abu Bakr suggested ransoming them. The Prophet, peace be upon him, accepted Abu Bakr\'s opinion, but revelation descended in agreement with Umar\'s view. As for the spoils of war, the chapter of Al-Anfal was revealed concerning them.\",\"text\":\"The Battle of Badr (the Great) and the Victory of the Muslims.\\n\\nThe Messenger of God, peace be upon him, dispatched a group of Muslims to intercept the Quraysh caravan coming from Syria, which was led by Abu Sufyan. Abu Sufyan later learned of the Muslims\' departure and sent a message to Quraysh calling for their aid to rescue their trade. He also changed his route to save the caravan. Then, the Muslims and the polytheists met at Badr, a place between Mecca and Medina, and closer to Medina than Mecca. The number of polytheists was nearly a thousand, while the number of Muslims was over three hundred. The battle began with the famous duel, then the fighting started and was intense. Prominent leaders of Quraysh, such as Abu Jahl and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and others were killed, with their total dead reaching seventy men and the same number taken captive. Fourteen Muslims were killed, and some say sixteen. Thus, a great victory was achieved by the Muslims. God Almighty aided them and sent angels to fight alongside them. Regarding the captives, Umar suggested killing them, while Abu Bakr suggested ransoming them. The Prophet, peace be upon him, accepted Abu Bakr\'s opinion, but revelation descended in agreement with Umar\'s view. As for the spoils of war, the chapter of Al-Anfal was revealed concerning them.\",\"reference\":\"Event #59 | CE 624 | Hijri 2 | Badr | https://dorar.net/history/event/59\",\"type\":\"story\",\"confidence_score\":8}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[5],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"The Battle of Badr was a pivotal event in Islamic history. Allah says the Messenger of God dispatched a group of Muslims to intercept a Quraysh caravan led by Abu Sufyan. The Muslims and polytheists met at Badr, with nearly a thousand polytheists and over three hundred Muslims. The battle was intense, resulting in the deaths of seventy polytheists and the same number taken captive. Fourteen Muslims were killed, and some say sixteen. Allah aided the Muslims, and angels fought alongside them. The Prophet accepted Abu Bakr\'s opinion to ransom the captives, but revelation later agreed with Umar\'s view to kill them. The chapter of Al-Anfal was revealed concerning the spoils of war.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"story\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"story\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":14}}', '2026-03-04 06:09:32', '2026-03-04 00:09:32'),
(86, '999599259627866f1290c5f37cc46e5afaf71e30c0c00cd51b06bb5e94174f46', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocation for At-Tashahhud (sitting in prayer) #52\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #73\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((التَّحِيَّاتُ لِلَّهِ، وَالصَّلَواتُ، وَالطَّيِّباتُ، السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ وَرَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ، السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى عِبَادِ اللَّهِ الصَّالِحِينَ. أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّداً عَبْدُهُ وَرَسولُهُ)).\",\"english\":\"(At-tahiyyat is for Allah. All acts of worship and good deeds are for Him.  Peace and the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon you O Prophet.  Peace be upon us and all of Allah’s righteous servants. I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger.)(At-tahiyyat: all words which indicate the glorification of Allah.  His eternal existence, His perfection and His sovereignty.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocation for At-Tashahhud (sitting in prayer) #52\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ عِلْماً نافِعاً، وَرِزْقاً طَيِّباً، وَعَمَلاً مُتَقَبَّلاً)) بَعْدَ السّلامِ مِنْ صَلاَةِ الفَجْرِ.\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial and sustenance which is good, and deeds which are acceptable.)(To be said after giving salam for the fajr prayer)\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #73\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[6,8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Recommended supplication(s):\\n1. (At-tahiyyat is for Allah. All acts of worship and good deeds are for Him. Peace and the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon you O Prophet. Peace be upon us and all of Allah’s righteous servants. I bear witness that non...\\n   Arabic: ((التَّحِيَّاتُ لِلَّهِ، وَالصَّلَواتُ، وَالطَّيِّباتُ، السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ وَرَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ، السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى عِبَادِ اللَّهِ الصَّالِحِينَ. أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّداً عَبْدُهُ وَرَسولُهُ)).\\n   Reference: Invocation for At-Tashahhud (sitting in prayer) #52\\n2. (O Allah, I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial and sustenance which is good, and deeds which are acceptable.)(To be said after giving salam for the fajr prayer)\\n   Arabic: ((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ عِلْماً نافِعاً، وَرِزْقاً طَيِّباً، وَعَمَلاً مُتَقَبَّلاً)) بَعْدَ السّلامِ مِنْ صَلاَةِ الفَجْرِ.\\n   Reference: What to say after completing the prayer #73\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"local\",\"provider_model\":\"deterministic\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":2,\"top_selected_score\":20}}', '2026-03-04 06:30:18', '2026-03-04 00:30:18'),
(87, '9a9961389b6951b992d84ac811046f9ec3f07c29cab12f90d2b50ca0ab1a1670', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"guidance\",\"intent\":\"dua_adhkar_lookup\",\"router_category\":\"dua\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #55\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #57\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #58\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #63\"},{\"dataset_id\":3,\"dataset_name\":\"Dua and Adhkar Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"dua\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #66\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُــمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عَذَابِ الْقَبْرِ، وَمِنْ عَذَابِ جَهَنَّمَ، وَمِنْ فِتْنَةِ الْمَحْيَا وَالْمَمَاتِ، وَمِنْ شَرِّ فِتْنَةِ الْمَسِيحِ الدَّجَّالِ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, I take refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, from the torment of the Fire, from the trials and tribulations of life and death and from the evil affliction of Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal.)(Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal: among the great signs of the last hour and the greatest trials to befall mankind, which every Prophet has warned about.  Most of mankind will follow him. He will appear from Asbahan, Iran at the time when the Muslims will conquer Constantinople.  He will be given special powers and will make the truth seem false and vice versa.  He will claim to be righteous and then he will claim prophethood and finally, divinity.  From his features is that he will be blind in his right eye which is a definite proof that contradicts his claim to be Allah as it is a sign of imperfection.  The word Kafir will be written between his eyes which every believer, literate or illiterate will recognise.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #55\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي ظُلْماً كَثِيراً، وَلاَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنوبَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، فَاغْفِرْ لِي مَغْفِرَةً مِنْ عِنْدِكَ وَارْحَمْنِي، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الغَفورُ الرَّحيمُ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, I have indeed oppressed my soul excessively and none can forgive sin except You, so forgive me a forgiveness from Yourself and have mercy upon me.  Surely, You are The Most-Forgiving, The Most-Merciful.)(From Yourself: i.e. from Your innermost grace without deserving it and a forgiveness which is befitting to your tremendous generosity.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #57\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِي مَا قَدَّمْتُ، وَمَا أَخَّرْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَرْتُ، وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَفْتُ، وَمَا أَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّي. أَنْتَ الْمُقَدِّمُ، وَأَنْتَ الْمُؤَخِّرُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, forgive me for those sins which have come to pass as well as those which shall come to pass, and those I have committed in secret as well as those I have made public, and where I have exceeded all bounds as well as those things about which You are more knowledgeable. You are Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir.  None has the right to be worshipped except You.)(Meaning of Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu-akhkhir: Allah puts forward and favours whom He wills from amongst His creation just as He defers and holds back whom He wills in accordance to His wisdom.  E.g.  Favouring man over the rest of creation, favouring the Prophets over the rest of mankind, favouring Muhammad  over all the Prophets and Messengers…etc.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #58\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ يَا أَللَّهُ بِأَنَّكَ الْوَاحِدُ الْأَحَدُ الصَّمَدُ الَّذِي لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يولَدْ، وَلَمْ يَكنْ لَهُ كُفُواً أَحَدٌ، أَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِي ذُنُوبِي إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِّيمُ)).\",\"english\":\"(O Allah, I ask You O Allah, as You are The One, The Only, AS-Samad, The One who begets not, nor was He begotten and there is none like unto Him that You forgive me my sins for verily You are The Oft-Forgiving, Most-Merciful.)(AS-Samad: The Self-Sufficient Master, Possessor of perfect attributes whom all of creation turn to in all their needs.)\",\"reference\":\"Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #63\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4},{\"arabic\":\"((أَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ (ثَلاَثَاً) اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ السَّلاَمُ، وَمِنْكَ السَّلاَمُ، تَبَارَكْتَ يَا ذَا الْجَلاَلِ وَالْإِكْرَامِ)).\",\"english\":\"(I ask Allah for forgiveness.(three times) (O Allah, You are As-Salam and from You is all peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honour.) (AS-Salam: The One Who is free from all defects and deficiencies.))\",\"reference\":\"What to say after completing the prayer #66\",\"type\":\"dua\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[1,2,3,4,5],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Recommended supplication(s):\\n1. (O Allah, I take refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, from the torment of the Fire, from the trials and tribulations of life and death and from the evil affliction of Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal.)(Al-Maseeh Ad-Dajjal:...\\n   Arabic: ((اللَّهُــمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عَذَابِ الْقَبْرِ، وَمِنْ عَذَابِ جَهَنَّمَ، وَمِنْ فِتْنَةِ الْمَحْيَا وَالْمَمَاتِ، وَمِنْ شَرِّ فِتْنَةِ الْمَسِيحِ الدَّجَّالِ)).\\n   Reference: Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #55\\n2. (O Allah, I have indeed oppressed my soul excessively and none can forgive sin except You, so forgive me a forgiveness from Yourself and have mercy upon me. Surely, You are The Most-Forgiving, The Most-Merciful.)(From Yo...\\n   Arabic: ((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي ظُلْماً كَثِيراً، وَلاَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنوبَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ، فَاغْفِرْ لِي مَغْفِرَةً مِنْ عِنْدِكَ وَارْحَمْنِي، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الغَفورُ الرَّحيمُ)).\\n   Reference: Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #57\\n3. (O Allah, forgive me for those sins which have come to pass as well as those which shall come to pass, and those I have committed in secret as well as those I have made public, and where I have exceeded all bounds as wel...\\n   Arabic: ((اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِي مَا قَدَّمْتُ، وَمَا أَخَّرْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَرْتُ، وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُ، وَمَا أَسْرَفْتُ، وَمَا أَنْتَ أَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّي. أَنْتَ الْمُقَدِّمُ، وَأَنْتَ الْمُؤَخِّرُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ أَنْتَ)).\\n   Reference: Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #58\\n4. (O Allah, I ask You O Allah, as You are The One, The Only, AS-Samad, The One who begets not, nor was He begotten and there is none like unto Him that You forgive me my sins for verily You are The Oft-Forgiving, Most-Merc...\\n   Arabic: ((اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ يَا أَللَّهُ بِأَنَّكَ الْوَاحِدُ الْأَحَدُ الصَّمَدُ الَّذِي لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يولَدْ، وَلَمْ يَكنْ لَهُ كُفُواً أَحَدٌ، أَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِي ذُنُوبِي إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِّيمُ)).\\n   Reference: Invocations after the final Tash-ahhud and before ending the prayer #63\\n5. (I ask Allah for forgiveness.(three times) (O Allah, You are As-Salam and from You is all peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honour.) (AS-Salam: The One Who is free from all defects and deficiencies.))\\n   Arabic: ((أَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ (ثَلاَثَاً) اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ السَّلاَمُ، وَمِنْكَ السَّلاَمُ، تَبَارَكْتَ يَا ذَا الْجَلاَلِ وَالْإِكْرَامِ)).\\n   Reference: What to say after completing the prayer #66\\n\\nThese supplications are commonly recited during moments of need and remembrance.\",\"provider_used\":\"local\",\"provider_model\":\"deterministic\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"dua\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"dua\",\"reason\":\"explicit_source_lock\",\"candidate_count\":8,\"selected_count\":5,\"top_selected_score\":20}}', '2026-03-04 06:31:22', '2026-03-04 00:31:22'),
(88, '5178209611b35fc27f289f9669db980768b431176f5e7bc6b93d94128e22c1c2', '{\"status\":\"success\",\"out_of_scope\":false,\"message\":\"\",\"classification\":\"informational\",\"intent\":\"llm_router:general_islamic_guidance\",\"router_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"dataset\":{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"},\"datasets_used\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"type\":\"quran\",\"storage_type\":\"json\"}],\"sources\":[{\"dataset_id\":1,\"dataset_name\":\"Quran JSON Dataset\",\"dataset_type\":\"quran\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):246\"}],\"original_items\":[{\"arabic\":\"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلْمَلَإِ مِنۢ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰٓ إِذْ قَالُوا۟ لِنَبِىٍّ لَّهُمُ ٱبْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا نُّقَـٰتِلْ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِن كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْقِتَالُ أَلَّا تُقَـٰتِلُوا۟ ۖ قَالُوا۟ وَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نُقَـٰتِلَ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَدْ أُخْرِجْنَا مِن دِيَـٰرِنَا وَأَبْنَآئِنَا ۖ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوْا۟ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّنْهُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌۢ بِٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ\",\"english\":\"Have you not considered the assembly of the Children of Israel after [the time of] Moses when they said to a prophet of theirs, \\\"Send to us a king, and we will fight in the way of Allah \\\"? He said, \\\"Would you perhaps refrain from fighting if fighting was prescribed for you?\\\" They said, \\\"And why should we not fight in the cause of Allah when we have been driven out from our homes and from our children?\\\" But when fighting was prescribed for them, they turned away, except for a few of them. And Allah is Knowing of the wrongdoers.\",\"reference\":\"Surah Al-Baqarah (2):246\",\"type\":\"quran_ayah\",\"confidence_score\":4}],\"ranked_candidate_ids\":[8],\"related_scholar_answer\":false,\"ai_explanation\":\"Allah says in Surah Al-Baqarah (2):246 that the Children of Israel, after the time of Prophet Musa, asked a prophet to send a king so they could fight in the way of Allah. However, when fighting was prescribed for them, they turned away, except for a few of them. This shows that they were not willing to follow Allah\'s command when it became difficult.\",\"provider_used\":\"groq\",\"provider_model\":\"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\"cache_hit\":false,\"debug_routing\":{\"router_raw_category\":\"story\",\"router_confidence\":0,\"final_category\":\"general_islamic_guidance\",\"reason\":\"selector_category_confirmed\",\"candidate_count\":15,\"selected_count\":1,\"top_selected_score\":10}}', '2026-03-04 06:32:26', '2026-03-04 00:32:26');
