(55, 52, 'What is Ghusl?\r\n\r\nThe word ghusl (غسل) in Arabic literally means “washing.” In Islamic terminology, ghusl refers to the complete washing of the body with the intention of purification. It is different from ordinary bathing because it is done with a specific intention (niyyah) and includes certain mandatory actions.\r\n\r\nA normal shower may make the body clean physically, but without the intention and the correct procedure, it does not count as ghusl. That is why scholars emphasize that Muslims should learn the proper way to perform it.', NULL, 'public', 0, '2026-03-28 23:51:35', '2026-03-28 23:51:35'),
(56, 2, 'Allah will give EVERYTHING!!!', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jrzzg7a-bno', 'public', 0, '2026-03-30 12:50:28', '2026-03-30 12:50:28'),
