(75, 52, 'Saudi Supreme Court calls for sighting of new moon of 1447 Hijri month tomorrow, Sunday, May 17, 2026\r\nThe Supreme Court of Saudi Arabia has called on all citizens and residents to participate in the sighting of the new moon to mark the beginning of the month of 1447 Hijri.\r\n\r\nThe announcement highlights the significance of the month of Dhul Hijjah in Islam. It is during this holy month that millions of Muslims from all over the world gather in Mecca to perform the Hajj, one of the five pillars of Islam. In addition, the tenth day of Dhul Hijjah marks Eid al-Adha, a major Islamic festival commemorating the willingness of Prophet Ibrahim (A.) to sacrifice his son in obedience to Allah.\r\n\r\nThe Supreme Court has invited experts in astronomy and individuals with observation equipment to contribute to this effort and support the moon sighting process.', NULL, 'public', 0, '2026-05-17 15:23:20', '2026-05-17 15:23:20'),
